(window.LINGUA_BOOK=window.LINGUA_BOOK||{}).condense=Object.assign(window.LINGUA_BOOK.condense||{},{"part-003-slug-3-phonetics":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 3: Phonetics","zh":"第3章：语音学"},"summary":{"en":"Every language has a physical reality: a way of transmitting linguistic signals between people. This chapter introduces that reality by examining the body parts that languages use, the movements that create a linguistic signal, and the ways linguists categorize, describe, and notate these physical properties so that a language can be recorded and studied.","zh":"任何语言都具有物质现实，即以某种方式在人与人之间传递语言信号。本章从这一现实入手，考察语言所使用的身体部位、这些部位如何运动以产生语言信号，以及语言学家如何对语言的物理属性进行分类、描写与标写，从而使一门语言能够被记录和研究。"},"points":[{"en":"Languages differ not only in grammar but in the physical channel through which signals travel between people.","zh":"语言之间的差别不仅在语法，还在于信号在人与人之间传递时所借助的物质通道。"},{"en":"The chapter examines the body parts used for language and how they move to create a signal.","zh":"本章考察语言所使用的身体部位，以及这些部位如何运动以产生语言信号。"},{"en":"Linguists categorize, describe, and notate the physical properties of language so that information can be recorded.","zh":"语言学家对语言的物理属性进行分类、描写与标写，以便记录并查阅有关某一语言的信息。"},{"en":"Readers should be able to identify the locations and functions of anatomy relevant to spoken and signed articulation.","zh":"读者应能指出与口语和手语发音相关的身体结构的位置与功能。"},{"en":"Readers should also be able to give articulatory descriptions of phones and signs and read common IPA symbols.","zh":"读者还应能对音素与手语符号作出发音描写，并识别国际音标中的许多常用符号。"}],"terms":[{"en":"modality","zh":"模态","defEn":"The way a language is physically produced and perceived by its users.","defZh":"一门语言在物理上被发出并被感知的方式，如口语的声学—听觉模态。"},{"en":"articulation","zh":"发音（构音）","defEn":"Using parts of the body to produce a linguistic signal.","defZh":"运用身体各部位发出语言信号的过程，是语音传递链条的起点。"},{"en":"International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)","zh":"国际音标","defEn":"A notational system whose symbols are used to represent speech sounds.","defZh":"一套用于标写语音的符号系统，语言学家借以记录各种语言的音素。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"A central aspect of any language is its physical reality in the world: the way linguistic signals are transmitted from one person to another. This chapter approaches that reality from three directions. It begins with the parts of the human body that languages rely on, then considers how those parts move in order to create a linguistic signal, and finally asks how linguists categorize, describe, and notate these physical properties so that information about a language can be recorded and later consulted. Speech and sign are both treated as physical phenomena with describable properties.","zh":"任何语言都有一个核心面向，即它在世界中的物质现实：语言信号如何从一个人传递到另一个人。本章从三个方向切入这一现实：先看语言所依赖的人体各部位，再看这些部位如何运动以产生语言信号，最后讨论语言学家如何对上述物理属性进行分类、描写和标写，从而能够记录并随时查阅有关一门语言的信息。口语与手语在这里都被视为具有可描写属性的物质现象。"},{"en":"By the end of the chapter, readers should be able to identify the locations and functions of the parts of human anatomy relevant to the articulation of spoken and signed languages, provide articulatory descriptions of given examples of phones and signs, and identify the meanings of many common symbols from the International Phonetic Alphabet. These skills support the later study of how sounds pattern in the grammar of a language.","zh":"学完本章，读者应能达到以下目标：指出与口语和手语发音相关的各人体结构的位置与功能；对给定的音素和手语符号实例作出发音描写；识别国际音标中许多常用符号所表示的音值。这些技能为后续学习语音在语言语法中的组合与分布规律打下基础。"}]},"chapter-018-slug-3-1-modality":{"title":{"en":"3.1 Modality","zh":"3.1 模态"},"summary":{"en":"Communication runs from an intended message, through articulation, to a physical signal that another person perceives and interprets. The full chain defines a language's modality. Spoken languages are vocal-auditory and signed languages manual-visual, while other modalities and multimodal communication also exist. The term phonetics now covers the study of linguistic modality in general, with articulatory, perceptual, and acoustic subfields.","zh":"交际从说话者心中的意图信息开始，经由发音产生物质性的语言信号，再由他人感知并解读，这一完整链条界定了一门语言的模态。口语属于声学—听觉模态，手语属于手部—视觉模态，而 phonetics（语音学）这一术语如今泛指对语言模态的研究。"},"points":[{"en":"Communication begins with an intended message and ends when another person reconstructs it through perception.","zh":"交际始于说话者想要表达的信息，终于听者通过感知重建这一信息。"},{"en":"Articulation gives the message physical reality, producing sound waves or light waves as the linguistic signal.","zh":"发音使信息获得物质现实，产生声波或光波作为语言信号。"},{"en":"The modality of a language is the whole chain from articulation to perception, or how it is produced and perceived.","zh":"语言的模态指从发音到感知的完整链条，即该语言如何被发出、又如何被感知。"},{"en":"Spoken languages are vocal-auditory; signed languages are manual-visual, articulated by hands and arms and received visually.","zh":"口语属于声学—听觉模态；手语属于手部—视觉模态，由手和手臂发出，由视觉系统接收。"},{"en":"Much communication is multimodal, since speech often accompanies gesture and facial expression, which carry meaning in signed languages.","zh":"许多交际是多模态的：口语常伴随手势与面部表情，而在手语中面部表情本身也承载意义。"},{"en":"Phonetics, from the Greek word for sound or voice, now names the study of linguistic modality in general.","zh":"phonetics 源自希腊语中表示声音或嗓音的词，如今指对语言模态的总体研究。"}],"terms":[{"en":"modality","zh":"模态","defEn":"The chain from articulation to perception, or how a language is produced and perceived.","defZh":"从发音到感知的完整链条，即一门语言如何被发出、又如何被感知。"},{"en":"articulation","zh":"发音（构音）","defEn":"Movements and configurations of body parts that give a message physical reality.","defZh":"身体各部位的运动与配置，使意图信息获得物质现实并成为可传递的信号。"},{"en":"vocal-auditory","zh":"声学—听觉（模态）","defEn":"The modality of spoken languages: articulated with the vocal tract and received by hearing.","defZh":"口语所属的模态：用声道发出，由听觉系统接收，中间以声波传递。"},{"en":"manual-visual","zh":"手部—视觉（模态）","defEn":"The modality of signed languages: articulated by hands and arms and received visually.","defZh":"手语所属的模态：由手和手臂发出，以光波传递，由视觉系统接收。"},{"en":"tactile signing","zh":"触觉手语","defEn":"A signing practice in which the perceiver feels the signs rather than seeing them.","defZh":"一种手语使用方式，接收者以触摸而非观看的方式感知手语符号。"},{"en":"articulatory phonetics","zh":"发音语音学","defEn":"The study of how the body creates a linguistic signal.","defZh":"研究身体如何发出语言信号的语音学分支，是本章集中讨论的内容。"}],"examples":[{"text":"English and Cantonese","noteEn":"Spoken languages cited as having the vocal-auditory modality.","noteZh":"原文举出的口语例子，属于声学—听觉模态。"},{"text":"American Sign Language and Chinese Sign Language","noteEn":"Signed languages cited as having the manual-visual modality.","noteZh":"原文举出的手语例子，属于手部—视觉模态。"},{"text":"φωνή (phōnḗ)","noteEn":"Ancient Greek word meaning sound or voice, the source of phonetics.","noteZh":"古希腊语中表示声音或嗓音的词，是 phonetics 一词的词源。"}],"body":[{"en":"An act of communication normally starts when one person constructs an intended message in the mind and then gives it physical reality through articulation, the movements and configurations of their body parts. This produces a physical linguistic signal such as sound waves for spoken languages or light waves for signed languages. Another person receives, senses, and processes that signal through perception, and so reconstructs the intended message. The entire chain from articulation to perception is called the modality of the language: how it is produced and perceived.","zh":"一次交际通常始于一个人在心中构建想要表达的信息，随后通过发音——即身体各部位的运动与配置——使这一信息获得物质现实。由此产生物质性的语言信号：口语是声波，手语是光波。另一个人通过感知接收、感觉并加工这一信号，从而重建原初的意图信息。从发音到感知的这一完整物质现实链条，就称为该语言的模态，也就是这门语言如何被发出、又如何被感知。"},{"en":"Spoken languages like English and Cantonese are vocal, because they are articulated with the vocal tract; acoustic, because sound waves carry them; and auditory, because the hearing system receives them, a combination usually shortened to vocal-auditory. Signed languages such as American Sign Language and Chinese Sign Language are instead manual, photic, and visual, giving the label manual-visual. Other modalities are possible but are not treated here, one example being the manual-somatic modality of tactile signing, used by some deafblind people who feel rather than see the signs. Communication is also frequently multimodal, since spoken language is commonly accompanied by shrugging, facial expressions, and hand gestures that convey emphasis, attitude, or turn-taking, while facial expressions carry essential meaning in many signed languages.","zh":"英语、粤语等口语是发声的，因为用声道发音；是声学的，因为靠声波传递；是听觉的，因为由听觉系统接收，这一组合通常简称为声学—听觉模态。美国手语、中国手语等手语则相反，是手部的、光学的、视觉的，因而称为手部—视觉模态。其他模态虽有可能存在，但本书不予讨论，例如某些聋盲人群体的触觉手语采用手部—躯体模态，接收者以触摸而非观看的方式感知手语。交际还常常是多模态的：口语通常伴随耸肩、面部表情和手势，用以传达强调、态度或话轮转换等信息，而在许多手语中，面部表情本身就承载关键意义。"},{"en":"The word phonetics descends from the Ancient Greek φωνή (phōnḗ), meaning sound or voice. For a long time linguistics attended almost exclusively to spoken languages, so the study of language modality was named phonetics after the vocal-auditory modality. Because all human languages share similar underlying properties regardless of modality, the term now refers to the study of linguistic modality in general. Three subfields correspond to the components of modality: articulatory phonetics studies how the body creates a signal, perceptual phonetics studies how the body perceives and processes it, and acoustic phonetics studies linguistic sound waves. No comparable subfield yet studies the physical properties of light waves in the manual-visual modality.","zh":"phonetics 一词源自古希腊语的 φωνή（phōnḗ），意为声音或嗓音。长期以来语言学几乎只关注口语，因此对语言模态的研究便依声学—听觉模态而被命名为 phonetics。由于所有人类语言无论模态如何都具有相似的底层属性，这一术语如今泛指对语言模态的研究。模态的三个环节各对应一个分支：发音语音学研究身体如何发出信号，感知语音学研究身体如何接收并加工信号，声学语音学研究语言的声波。目前还没有相应的分支来研究手部—视觉模态中光波的物理属性。"}]},"chapter-019-slug-3-2-speech-articulators":{"title":{"en":"3.2 Speech articulators","zh":"3.2 发音器官"},"summary":{"en":"Spoken language is articulated mainly in the vocal tract, which linguists depict with a midsagittal diagram. Its three open regions are the oral cavity, pharynx, and nasal cavity, with the trachea supplying most speech air. Individual speech sounds are called phones or segments, and each language counts as phones only those sounds that appear in ordinary words.","zh":"口语主要在声道中发音，语言学家用矢状剖面图标示声道。声道有三个开阔区域：口腔、咽腔和鼻腔，多数语音的气流来自气管。单个语音单位称为音素或音段，每种语言只把出现在普通词中的音算作自己的音素，打嗝、哼鼻等非语音响声则不算。"},"points":[{"en":"For spoken language, articulation happens primarily in the vocal tract, using the lips, tongue, and mouth and throat.","zh":"就口语而言，发音主要发生在声道中，使用双唇、舌头以及口腔和咽喉的其他部位。"},{"en":"A midsagittal diagram depicts the vocal tract as if the head were split between the eyes, lips on the left.","zh":"矢状剖面图把头部设想为沿两眼之间纵向剖开，并约定唇部在左、后脑在右。"},{"en":"The three open regions are the oral cavity, the pharynx behind the tongue, and the nasal cavity above them.","zh":"三个开阔区域是口腔、舌后的咽腔，以及位于口腔与咽腔上方的鼻腔。"},{"en":"The pharynx splits into the trachea, which leads to the lungs, and the esophagus, which is irrelevant to phonetics.","zh":"咽腔底部向下分为两条管道：通向肺部的气管，以及同语音学无关、通向胃部的食管。"},{"en":"Individual speech sounds are called phones or segments, and every language has its own inventory of them.","zh":"单个语音单位称为音素或音段，每种语言都拥有各自不同的音素清单。"},{"en":"A sound counts as a phone only if it appears in ordinary words, not in marginal expressions or non-speech noises.","zh":"一个音只有出现在普通词中才算作音素，边缘性词语或非语音的响声都不算。"}],"terms":[{"en":"vocal tract","zh":"声道","defEn":"The system of lips, tongue, mouth, and throat where spoken articulation happens.","defZh":"由双唇、舌头、口腔与咽喉构成的系统，是口语发音主要发生的部位。"},{"en":"midsagittal diagram","zh":"矢状剖面图","defEn":"A drawing of the head as if split down the middle between the eyes.","defZh":"把头部设想为沿两眼之间纵向剖开后所绘的示意图，用于标示声道各部位。"},{"en":"oral cavity","zh":"口腔","defEn":"The inside of the mouth, running from the lips to the back of the tongue.","defZh":"口腔内部的空间，从双唇向后延伸到舌根，是声道中重要的开阔区域。"},{"en":"pharynx","zh":"咽腔","defEn":"The region behind the tongue that forms the upper part of the throat.","defZh":"位于舌后方的区域，构成我们通常所说的咽喉的上部。"},{"en":"nasal cavity","zh":"鼻腔","defEn":"The open space above the oral cavity and pharynx, from nostrils to pharynx.","defZh":"位于口腔与咽腔上方、从鼻孔向后并向下通向咽腔的开阔空间。"},{"en":"trachea","zh":"气管","defEn":"The windpipe, which leads down to the lungs and supplies most speech air.","defZh":"又称风管，向下通向肺部，是大多数口语发音所用气流的来源。"}],"examples":[{"text":"spill, slip, lisp, and lips","noteEn":"Four English words containing the same four phones in different orders.","noteZh":"四个英语词，包含相同的四个音素，只是排列顺序不同。"},{"text":"[θ]","noteEn":"A sound articulated with the tongue between the teeth, frequent in English.","noteZh":"舌尖置于齿间发出的音，在英语中相当常见，在多数其他语言中却很罕见。"},{"text":"alveolar click [!] and the lateral click [ǁ]","noteEn":"Clicks found in Hadza and isiZulu but not counted as phones in English.","noteZh":"见于哈扎语和祖鲁语的搭嘴音，在英语中不算音素，尽管英语者会非语言地使用。"},{"text":"Ugh, I can’t believe you’re eating that","noteEn":"A marginal expression whose gravelly sound is not otherwise found in English words.","noteZh":"一句边缘性表达，其中粗哑的音响并不出现在其他英语词中，故不算英语音素。"}],"body":[{"en":"Articulation means using parts of the body to produce a language signal, and for spoken language it happens mainly in the vocal tract, using the lips, tongue, and other parts of the mouth and throat. Linguists often picture that tract with a midsagittal diagram, which shows the inside of the head as if it were split down the middle between the eyes. By convention the diagram is oriented with the nostrils and lips on the left and the back of the head on the right.","zh":"发音指运用身体部位产生语言信号；就口语而言，发音主要发生在声道中，使用双唇、舌头以及口腔和咽喉的其他部位。语言学家常用矢状剖面图来描绘声道，它把头部内部设想为沿两眼之间纵向剖开。按惯例，图的方向是鼻孔与双唇在左、后脑在右。"},{"en":"Three open regions of the vocal tract matter most. The oral cavity is the inside of the mouth, from the lips to the back of the tongue; the pharynx lies behind the tongue and forms the upper part of the throat; the nasal cavity is the space above both, running from the nostrils backward and down to the pharynx. These are general terms without precise boundaries. At its bottom the pharynx splits into two tubes: the trachea, or windpipe, leading to the lungs, and the esophagus, leading to the stomach. Phonetics can ignore the esophagus, but the trachea matters because most spoken language is articulated with air coming from the lungs.","zh":"声道中有三个最重要的开阔区域。口腔即嘴的内部，从双唇向后直到舌根；咽腔位于舌的后方，构成咽喉上部；鼻腔则是位于二者上方的空间，从鼻孔向后并向下通向咽腔。这些都是笼统的说法，彼此之间并没有精确的界线。咽腔底部向下分为两条管道：一条是通向肺部的气管（又称风管），另一条是通向胃部的食管。语音学无需关注食管，但气管很重要，因为大多数口语都是用来自肺部的气流发音的。"},{"en":"Linguists call individual speech sounds phones or segments, roughly individual units of speech that can be part of a word in a given language. The English words spill, slip, lisp, and lips each contain the same four phones in different orders, though a phone may vary slightly depending on its position. Every language has its own inventory: [θ] is frequent in English but rare elsewhere, while Hadza and isiZulu have clicks such as [!] and [ǁ] that English does not count as phones, even though English speakers use them non-linguistically. The criterion is whether a sound appears in ordinary words, so marginal expressions like ugh do not qualify, and neither do burps, snorts, or raspberries, though such sounds can still convey non-linguistic meaning.","zh":"语言学家把单个语音称为音素或音段，大致相当于在某一语言中能够充当词的一部分的独立语音单位。英语词 spill、slip、lisp 和 lips 各自都含有相同的四个音素，只是顺序不同；不过同一音素在不同位置上发音会略有变化。每种语言都有各自的音素清单：[θ] 在英语中很常见，在多数其他语言中却很罕见；而哈扎语和祖鲁语有 [!] 和 [ǁ] 这样的搭嘴音，英语并不把它们算作音素，尽管一些英语使用者会在非语言层面用它们表示不满或催促。判断标准是该音是否出现在普通词中，因此像 ugh 这样的边缘性表达不算，打嗝、哼鼻、弹舌之类的响声也不算，尽管这些非语音的声音仍能传达非语言的意义。"}]},"chapter-020-slug-3-3-describing-consonants-place-and-phonation":{"title":{"en":"3.3 Describing consonants: Place and phonation","zh":"3.3 描述辅音：发音部位与发声"},"summary":{"en":"Consonants are phones produced with relatively narrow constrictions in the vocal tract, made when an active or lower articulator moves toward a passive or upper articulator. This section lists the active and passive articulators, shows how their adjectives combine into names for place of articulation, and treats shortened labels, bilabial, dental, interdental, and retroflex articulations, the glottal place, and voicing and phonation.","zh":"辅音是声道中形成较窄阻碍的音素，阻碍由一个主动（下部）发音器官移向一个被动（上部）发音器官而构成。本节列出各主动与被动发音器官，说明其形容词如何组合成发音部位名称，并讨论缩略称名、双唇、齿、齿间与卷舌等部位、声门部位，以及浊音与发声。"},"points":[{"en":"Active articulators range from the lower lip to the tongue tip, blade, front, back, root, and the epiglottis.","zh":"主动发音器官从下唇依次包括舌尖、舌叶、舌前、舌后、舌根以及会厌。"},{"en":"Place of articulation combines the active and passive adjectives, as in labiodental or dorsovelar.","zh":"发音部位由主动与被动发音器官的形容词组合而成，如唇齿音或舌背软腭音。"},{"en":"Many places are shortened to the passive term alone, while bilabial, interdental, and retroflex are special cases.","zh":"许多部位名称缩略为只保留被动器官的说法，而双唇、齿间与卷舌属于特殊情形。"},{"en":"Glottal consonants involve only the vocal folds and have no clear active or passive articulator.","zh":"声门辅音只涉及声带，没有明确的主动或被动发音器官。"},{"en":"Voicing is vocal fold vibration, while phonation is the broader manipulation of airflow by the vocal folds.","zh":"浊音指声带振动，而发声是声带调控气流的更宽泛范畴。"}],"terms":[{"en":"active articulator","zh":"主动发音器官","defEn":"The moving or lower articulator that approaches another part of the vocal tract.","defZh":"发音时主动移动的下部器官，它向声道另一部位靠近并形成阻碍。"},{"en":"passive articulator","zh":"被动发音器官","defEn":"The target or upper articulator toward which the active articulator moves.","defZh":"主动发音器官所趋近的目标器官，即位置较为固定的上部发音器官。"},{"en":"place of articulation","zh":"发音部位","defEn":"The combination of an active articulator and a passive articulator in a consonant.","defZh":"辅音发音时主动发音器官与被动发音器官共同构成的部位。"},{"en":"bilabial","zh":"双唇音","defEn":"A consonant articulated with both lips moving toward each other as mutual targets.","defZh":"双唇互为运动目标而构成的辅音，两唇大致同等主动地靠近。"},{"en":"voicing","zh":"浊音","defEn":"Phonation in which airflow through the glottis causes the vocal folds to vibrate.","defZh":"气流通过声门时使声带振动的一种发声状态，与清音相对。"},{"en":"phonation","zh":"发声","defEn":"The manipulation of airflow through the vocal tract by the vocal folds in different ways.","defZh":"声带以不同方式调控通过声道气流的总范畴，范围大于浊音。"}],"examples":[{"text":"pin and fin","noteEn":"Both begin with labial consonants, since the lower lip is the active articulator.","noteZh":"二者均以唇音起首，因为下唇是主动发音器官。"},{"text":"thin and chin","noteEn":"These begin with laminal consonants, and are therefore also coronal.","noteZh":"这两个词以舌叶辅音起首，因而也属于舌前音。"},{"text":"su 'fire' and zu 'you'","noteEn":"Basque distinguishes these words by tongue tip versus tongue blade.","noteZh":"巴斯克语用舌尖与舌叶的对立区分这两个词。"},{"text":"he and who","noteEn":"Both begin with glottal consonants, but the lips are spread for he and rounded for who.","noteZh":"二者均以声门辅音起首，但 he 全程展唇，who 全程圆唇。"}],"body":[{"en":"Consonants are phones made with a relatively narrow constriction somewhere in the vocal tract. The moving part is the active or lower articulator, and its target is the passive or upper articulator. Listed from front to back, the active articulators are the lower lip, the tongue tip, the tongue blade, the tongue front, the tongue back, the tongue root, and the epiglottis, with matching adjectives such as labial, apical, laminal, coronal, dorsal, radical, and epiglottal.","zh":"辅音是在声道某处形成较窄阻碍的音素。移动的一方是主动（下部）发音器官，其目标则是相应的被动（上部）发音器官。主动发音器官由前到后依次为下唇、舌尖、舌叶、舌前、舌后、舌根和会厌，对应的形容词为唇、舌尖、舌叶、舌前、舌背、舌根和会厌。"},{"en":"The passive articulators run from the upper lip and upper teeth back through the alveolar ridge, the postalveolar region, the hard palate, the velum, the uvula, and the pharyngeal wall, with the adjectives labial, dental, alveolar, postalveolar, palatal, velar, uvular, and pharyngeal. A place of articulation combines both adjectives, the active one first without its ending, then a linking -o-, then the passive adjective, giving names such as labiodental for fin and dorsovelar for kin.","zh":"被动发音器官由前到后为上唇、上齿、齿龈、齿龈后区、硬腭、软腭、小舌和咽壁，对应的形容词为唇、齿、齿龈、齿龈后、腭、软腭、小舌和咽。发音部位把两个形容词组合起来，先写去掉词尾的主动器官形容词，再加连接元音 -o-，最后是被动器官形容词，于是 fin 的词首音为唇齿音，kin 的词首音为舌背软腭音。"},{"en":"Not every pairing of articulators is possible or attested. Frequently used places are shortened, usually to the passive adjective, so apicoalveolar becomes alveolar and dorsovelar becomes velar. Consonants made with both lips are called bilabial rather than labiolabial. Dentals come in a laminodental type and an interdental type, and postalveolars in a plain type and a retroflex type with the tongue tip curled back.","zh":"并非所有发音器官的配对都可行或见于语言。常用的部位名称往往缩略，通常只保留被动器官的形容词，因此舌尖齿龈音通常只说齿龈音，舌背软腭音只说软腭音。双唇都参与的辅音称为双唇音，而不说唇唇音。齿音有舌叶齿音与齿间音两类，齿龈后音也有普通与舌尖后卷的卷舌两类。"},{"en":"Glottal consonants, such as the first sound of he and who, consist only of vocal fold articulation, have no clear active or passive articulator, and take on aspects of neighbouring vowels. The vocal folds also regulate airflow for most sounds. Their vibration is called voicing, so a phone with it is voiced and one without it is voiceless; the broader shaping of airflow by the vocal folds is phonation.","zh":"声门辅音如 he 与 who 的词首音只由声带的运动构成，没有明确的主动或被动发音器官，并会吸收邻近元音的特征。声带也为大多数音调控气流。声带振动称为浊音，有振动的音是浊音，没有的是清音；声带调控气流的更大范畴称为发声，本书只讨论浊与清两种发声。"}]},"chapter-021-slug-3-4-describing-consonants-manner":{"title":{"en":"3.4 Describing consonants: Manner","zh":"3.4 描述辅音：发音方法"},"summary":{"en":"Manner of articulation describes how air flows through the vocal tract, depending on the size and shape of the constriction between the articulators. This section defines oral and nasal stops, including plosives, fricatives, central and lateral approximants, affricates, taps, and trills, groups consonants into obstruents, sonorants, and continuants, and then combines phonation, place, and manner into a full description.","zh":"发音方法描述气流如何在声道中通过，取决于发音器官之间阻碍的大小与形状。本节界定口塞音与鼻塞音，以及爆破音、擦音、央近音与边近音、塞擦音、闪音和颤音，并把辅音归为阻塞音、响音与持续音，最后把发声、发音部位与发音方法三者组合成完整描写。"},"points":[{"en":"Manner of articulation describes how air flows through the vocal tract given the size and shape of the constriction.","zh":"发音方法描述在特定阻碍大小与形状下气流如何通过声道。"},{"en":"Stops make a complete closure; a raised velum gives oral stops and a lowered velum nasal stops.","zh":"塞音形成完全闭塞；软腭抬起形成口塞音，软腭下降形成鼻塞音。"},{"en":"Fricatives have a narrow constriction producing turbulent frication, while approximants have little or no frication.","zh":"擦音阻碍狭窄，产生湍流性摩擦；近音则几乎没有摩擦。"},{"en":"An affricate is a plosive whose closure is released slowly, giving it a brief fricated release.","zh":"塞擦音是缓慢除阻、因而带有短暂摩擦性除阻的爆破音。"},{"en":"Obstruents are oral stops, fricatives, and affricates; sonorants are nasal stops, approximants, taps, and trills.","zh":"阻塞音包括口塞音、擦音和塞擦音；响音包括鼻塞音、近音、闪音和颤音。"}],"terms":[{"en":"manner of articulation","zh":"发音方法","defEn":"How air flows through the vocal tract, based on the size and shape of the constriction.","defZh":"依据发音器官间阻碍的大小与形状而定的气流通过声道的方式。"},{"en":"plosive","zh":"爆破音","defEn":"An oral stop whose trapped air is released in a quick explosive burst.","defZh":"被阻住的气流在闭塞解除后以短促爆发方式释放的口塞音。"},{"en":"fricative","zh":"擦音","defEn":"A phone made with a narrow constriction that turns airflow into turbulent frication.","defZh":"发音器官靠近但不接触，使气流变为湍流摩擦而成的语音。"},{"en":"approximant","zh":"近音","defEn":"A phone whose articulators are far enough apart to create little or no frication.","defZh":"发音器官相距较远、几乎不产生摩擦的语音，如央近音与边近音。"},{"en":"affricate","zh":"塞擦音","defEn":"A plosive with a fricated release, created by releasing the closure slowly.","defZh":"通过缓慢除阻而在释放时带出短暂摩擦成分的一类爆破音。"},{"en":"obstruent","zh":"阻塞音","defEn":"The class of oral stops, fricatives, and affricates, which significantly obstruct airflow.","defZh":"由口塞音、擦音与塞擦音构成、对气流有明显阻碍的类别。"}],"examples":[{"text":"met","noteEn":"Its initial consonant is fully described as a voiced bilabial nasal stop, hence a sonorant.","noteZh":"其词首辅音完整描写为浊双唇鼻塞音，因而属于响音。"},{"text":"set","noteEn":"Its initial consonant is a voiceless alveolar fricative, an obstruent and a continuant.","noteZh":"其词首辅音是清齿龈擦音，既是阻塞音也是持续音。"},{"text":"czy 'if, whether' and trzy 'three'","noteEn":"Polish contrasts an affricate with a plosive followed by a fricative.","noteZh":"波兰语以塞擦音对立于爆破音加擦音的组合。"},{"text":"pero 'but' and perro 'dog'","noteEn":"Spanish distinguishes a tap in the middle of pero from a trill in perro.","noteZh":"西班牙语以 pero 中间的闪音对立于 perro 中的颤音。"}],"body":[{"en":"Manner of articulation classifies consonant phones by how air flows through the vocal tract, based on the size and shape of the constriction between the articulators. In a stop, the active articulator presses firmly against the passive articulator and blocks all airflow. If the velum is raised, air passes only through the oral cavity, giving an oral stop; if it is lowered, air also enters the nasal cavity, giving a nasal stop. Most oral stops are plosives, but ejectives, implosives, and clicks are also oral stops.","zh":"发音方法依据发音器官之间阻碍的大小与形状，按气流通过声道的方式给辅音分类。发塞音时主动发音器官紧压被动发音器官，完全阻断气流。软腭抬起时气流只经口腔，形成口塞音；软腭下降时气流也进入鼻腔，形成鼻塞音。多数口塞音是爆破音，但挤喉音、内爆音和搭嘴音也属于口塞音。"},{"en":"When the articulators come very close without touching, the narrow constriction makes airflow turbulent and noisy, a frication that sounds like hissing or buzzing; such phones are fricatives. If the articulators are far enough apart that little or no frication results, the phone is an approximant. Most approximants allow airflow through the middle of the oral cavity and are central approximants, while a lateral approximant diverts airflow along one or both sides of a central contact.","zh":"当发音器官十分接近但并未接触时，狭窄的阻碍使气流变得湍乱嘈杂，产生类似嘶嘶声或嗡嗡声的摩擦，这类语音就是擦音。若发音器官相距足够远、几乎不产生摩擦，则该语音是近音。多数近音的气流较不受阻地通过口腔中部，称为央近音；边近音则让气流沿舌部中央接触的一侧或两侧通过。"},{"en":"Releasing a plosive closure slowly creates a brief fricative-like sound, so the release is fricated; a plosive with such a release is an affricate. Telling a true affricate apart from a plosive followed by a fricative is difficult, and the contrast is marginal in English but robust in Polish. Beyond the scope of this textbook are taps, whose closure is so brief that airflow is barely interrupted, and trills, which resemble repeated taps.","zh":"缓慢释放爆破音的闭塞会产生短暂的类擦音成分，即摩擦性除阻；带有这种除阻的爆破音就是塞擦音。区分真正的塞擦音与爆破音加擦音的组合十分困难，这一对立在英语中很边缘，在波兰语中则较稳固。超出本书范围的是闪音与颤音：闪音的闭塞极短，气流几乎未被阻断；颤音类似反复的闪音。"},{"en":"These manners also form larger classes. Oral stops, fricatives, and affricates are obstruents, defined by a significant obstruction to airflow, while nasal stops, approximants, taps, and trills are sonorants. Fricatives and approximants, with continuous oral airflow, are continuants. A consonant is described in the order phonation, place, manner, so met begins with a voiced bilabial nasal stop and set with a voiceless alveolar fricative.","zh":"这些发音方法还构成更大的类别。口塞音、擦音与塞擦音合称阻塞音，其特征是总体上对气流有显著阻碍；鼻塞音、近音、闪音与颤音合称响音，气流经鼻腔或口腔时较为通畅。擦音与近音因口腔气流持续，合称持续音。辅音的描写顺序为发声、发音部位、发音方法，因此 met 的词首音是浊双唇鼻塞音，set 的词首音是清齿龈擦音。"}]},"chapter-022-slug-3-5-describing-vowels":{"title":{"en":"3.5 Describing vowels","zh":"3.5 描述元音"},"summary":{"en":"Vowel phones are categorized by the configuration of the tongue and lips during their articulation, which determines the vowel's overall quality; quality is more of a continuum than consonant categories, so it is divided into broad regions. This section covers height, backness, rounding, tenseness, nasality, and length, explains why frontness depends on height, and treats monophthongs, diphthongs, and triphthongs.","zh":"元音音素按发音时舌头与嘴唇的形态分类，由此决定元音的整体音质；音质比辅音的部位与方法更接近连续统，因而只能划分为若干主要区域。本节介绍舌位高低、前后、圆唇、松紧、鼻化与长短，说明前后位置为何取决于高低，并讨论单元音、双元音与三元音。"},"points":[{"en":"Height (high, mid, low) and backness (front, central, back) describe vertical and horizontal tongue position.","zh":"舌位高低（高、中、低）与前后（前、央、后）分别描写舌头的垂直与水平位置。"},{"en":"Rounding distinguishes rounded, spread, and neutral lips, with spread and neutral grouped as unrounded.","zh":"圆唇区分圆唇、展唇与中性唇形，展唇与中性合称非圆唇。"},{"en":"Tenseness depends on tongue root position: advanced for tense vowels and retracted for lax vowels.","zh":"松紧取决于舌根位置：舌根前伸为紧元音，舌根后缩为松元音。"},{"en":"Nasality separates oral vowels from nasal vowels according to whether the velum is raised or lowered.","zh":"鼻化依软腭抬起或下降，把元音区分为口元音与鼻元音。"},{"en":"Length separates long from short vowels, and long consonants are geminates as opposed to singletons.","zh":"长短区分长元音与短元音，长辅音称为叠辅音，与单辅音相对。"},{"en":"Monophthongs hold a steady quality, while diphthongs and triphthongs shift through two or three qualities.","zh":"单元音音质稳定，双元音与三元音则依次经过两个或三个音质。"}],"terms":[{"en":"vowel quality","zh":"元音音质","defEn":"The overall character of a vowel, determined by tongue and lip configuration.","defZh":"由发音时舌头与嘴唇的形态所决定的元音整体听感特征。"},{"en":"backness","zh":"舌位前后","defEn":"The horizontal position of the tongue, giving front, central, and back vowels.","defZh":"舌头的水平位置，据此把元音分为前元音、央元音和后元音。"},{"en":"rounding","zh":"圆唇","defEn":"The shape of the lips, which may be rounded, spread, or neutral.","defZh":"发音时双唇的形态，可分为圆唇、展唇与中性三种情况。"},{"en":"tenseness","zh":"松紧","defEn":"Whether the tongue root is advanced for a tense vowel or retracted for a lax vowel.","defZh":"依舌根前伸或后缩而定的元音特征，使元音分为紧与松。"},{"en":"nasality","zh":"鼻化","defEn":"Whether a vowel is oral, with a raised velum, or nasal, with a lowered velum.","defZh":"依软腭抬起或下降而定，把元音分为口元音与鼻元音的特征。"},{"en":"diphthong","zh":"双元音","defEn":"A vowel phone that begins with one articulation and shifts quickly into another.","defZh":"从一种发音状态开始、并迅速滑向另一状态的元音音素。"}],"examples":[{"text":"beat and bat","noteEn":"Beat has a high vowel and bat a low vowel; both are front.","noteZh":"beat 含高元音，bat 含低元音；二者都是前元音。"},{"text":"ii 'good' and i 'stomach'","noteEn":"Japanese contrasts a long vowel in ii with a short vowel in i, with the same quality.","noteZh":"日语以 ii 的长元音对立于 i 的短元音，二者音质相同。"},{"text":"sammān 'honour' and samān 'equal'","noteEn":"Hindi contrasts a geminate bilabial nasal stop with a singleton in the middle of the word.","noteZh":"印地语以词中的叠双唇鼻塞音对立于单辅音。"},{"text":"rượu 'alcohol'","noteEn":"Vietnamese has a triphthong that moves through three vowel qualities.","noteZh":"越南语的该词含有依次经过三种元音音质的三元音。"}],"body":[{"en":"Vowel phones are described by the configuration of the tongue and lips during their articulation, which determines the vowel's overall quality. Quality is much more of a continuum than consonant place or manner: moving an articulator by less than a millimetre turns a stop into a fricative, yet that same distance makes no noticeable difference to a vowel. Vowel height refers to how high the tongue is, and backness to its horizontal position.","zh":"元音音素依发音时舌头与嘴唇的形态来描写，这一形态决定元音的整体音质。音质比辅音的部位与方法更接近连续统：发音器官移动不到一毫米就足以把塞音变成擦音，而同样的距离对元音却没有可察觉的影响。舌位高低指舌头的垂直位置，舌位前后则指其水平位置。"},{"en":"Backness cannot be defined in absolute terms. The human jaw is hinged, so lowering it also swings it backward and carries the tongue along, making it harder for a lowered tongue to reach as far forward as a high one. What counts as front therefore depends on vowel height. The possible combinations of height and backness thus form a skewed vowel space, drawn as an asymmetric quadrangle with the bottom left corner cut off.","zh":"舌位前后不能以绝对方式定义。人的下颌是铰接的，下颌下降时也向后摆动并带动舌头，使降低的舌头难以像高舌位那样前伸。因此，何谓前取决于元音的高低。于是高低与前后可能组合出的元音空间呈偏斜形状，通常画成一个被切掉左下角的不对称四边形。"},{"en":"Rounding concerns the shape of the lips: they may be compressed and protruded into a circle, thinly stretched into a smile, or in between, and spread and neutral configurations together count as unrounded. Tenseness depends on the tongue root, which may be advanced for a tense vowel or retracted for a lax vowel; many languages, such as Taba, need no such distinction, whereas English has tense and lax pairs. Nasality separates oral from nasal vowels, and length separates long from short vowels and geminates from singletons.","zh":"圆唇涉及双唇的形状：双唇可以收拢前突成圆形，可以拉平成微笑状，也可以处于中间状态，展唇与中性状态合称非圆唇。松紧取决于舌根：舌根前伸为紧元音，舌根后缩为松元音；许多语言如 Taba 无需这一区分，而英语有紧松配对的元音。鼻化区分口元音与鼻元音，长短区分长元音与短元音，以及叠辅音与单辅音。"},{"en":"Vowels that keep a stable pronunciation from beginning to end are monophthongs. Diphthongs begin with one articulation and shift quickly into another, and some languages even have triphthongs, which move through three vowel qualities. There is less consistency in the order of vowel descriptions than for consonants; a common order is height, backness, rounding, with nasality almost always last and tenseness or length usually first.","zh":"从头到尾发音相对稳定的元音是单元音。双元音从某一特定发音状态开始并迅速滑向另一状态；有些语言甚至有三元音，依次经过三种元音音质。元音描写的顺序不如辅音统一；常见顺序是高低、前后、圆唇，鼻化几乎总是放在最后，而松紧或长短通常放在最前。"}]},"chapter-023-slug-3-6-the-international-phonetic-alphabet":{"title":{"en":"3.6 The International Phonetic Alphabet","zh":"3.6 国际音标"},"summary":{"en":"Words are not always easy to divide into phones, and writing systems are too irregular and too language-specific to transcribe them reliably. Linguists therefore use the International Phonetic Alphabet, a standard symbol system first published in the late nineteenth century and still revised today. Transcriptions are placed in square brackets and may be broad or narrow. The section explains the IPA's guiding principles and shows how English consonants and vowels are transcribed.","zh":"词中的音素并不总能轻易切分，而书写系统又过于不规则、只服务于单一语言，无法可靠地标写语音。因此语言学家采用国际音标这套标准符号系统，它于19世纪末首次公布，至今仍在修订。标音写在方括号内，可宽可严。本节说明国际音标的组织原则与使用建议，并示范英语辅音和元音的标音。"},"points":[{"en":"Words are not always neatly divisible into phones; waveforms show that some words have clear boundaries while others do not.","zh":"词并不总能被整齐地切分为音素；波形图显示，有些词的音素边界清晰，有些则不然。"},{"en":"Because writing systems are inconsistent and language-specific, linguists transcribe phones with the International Phonetic Alphabet inside square brackets.","zh":"由于书写系统既不统一又只服务于单一语言，语言学家用国际音标在方括号内标写音素。"},{"en":"Transcription may be broad, giving only what is needed to distinguish words, or narrow, recording fine phonetic detail.","zh":"标音可宽可严：宽式标音只记录区分词所必需的信息，严式标音则记录细致的语音特征。"},{"en":"The IPA recommends typographic simplicity: choose upright symbols over rotated ones and use diacritics only when their meaning is crucial.","zh":"国际音标提倡排印上的简洁：能用正体符号就不用旋转符号，只有当附加符号的意义至关重要时才使用。"},{"en":"English consonants and vowels vary across dialects, so the transcriptions given are a rough North American baseline, not any single speaker.","zh":"英语的辅音和元音随方言而变，本节标音只是大致的北美基线，并不代表任何具体说话人。"}],"terms":[{"en":"International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)","zh":"国际音标","defEn":"A standard system of symbols used to transcribe the phones of any spoken language.","defZh":"一套用于标写任何口语语言音素的标准符号系统，由国际语音协会创制并不断修订。"},{"en":"transcription","zh":"标音","defEn":"A notation of the phones of a word, conventionally enclosed in square brackets.","defZh":"对词中音素的符号记录，按惯例写在方括号内，可宽可严。"},{"en":"diacritic","zh":"附加符号（变音符号）","defEn":"A special mark placed on or beside a symbol to modify its meaning.","defZh":"置于符号上下方或旁边以改变其含义的特殊标记，如送气符号与卷舌符号。"},{"en":"waveform","zh":"波形图","defEn":"A picture that graphically represents the air vibrations of sound waves.","defZh":"以图形方式表示声波所引起空气振动情况的图像，可用于观察音素边界。"},{"en":"affricate","zh":"塞擦音","defEn":"A phone with a stop closure followed by a fricated release, written with a tie-bar.","defZh":"先形成塞音闭塞、随后以摩擦方式除阻的音素，标写时用连音符把塞音与擦音符号连接起来。"},{"en":"rhotic","zh":"r 音类（rhotic）","defEn":"A class of consonants with great cross-linguistic variation, including English r.","defZh":"一类在跨语言比较中差异极大的辅音，英语中拼作 r 的辅音即属此类。"}],"examples":[{"text":"nab and wool","noteEn":"Waveforms for these English words differ in how clearly they can be segmented into phones.","noteZh":"原文用这两个英语词的波形图作对比：nab 的音素边界明显，wool 则平滑过渡、难以切分。"},{"text":"either, data, and route","noteEn":"English words that have more than one equally valid pronunciation.","noteZh":"原文举出的英语词，说明同一个词常有多种同样合理的读音。"},{"text":"[t͡ʃ]","noteEn":"The simplified transcription of the voiceless postalveolar affricate at the start of chin.","noteZh":"英语 chin 开头清龈后塞擦音的简化标音，省去了圆唇和后移两个附加符号。"},{"text":"witch and which","noteEn":"A pair distinguished by voiced [w] and voiceless [ʍ] for the few speakers who have both.","noteZh":"对少数仍区分这两个词的说话人而言，witch 用浊音 [w]，which 用清音 [ʍ]。"}],"body":[{"en":"Speech is a continuous physical signal, and dividing it into individual phones is not always straightforward. Waveforms of the English words nab and wool make the difference clear: nab shows abrupt transitions among three distinct regions, while wool runs smoothly from beginning to end with no obvious divisions. In this textbook words are segmented for you, but raw recordings of an unfamiliar language may leave the boundaries between phones uncertain.","zh":"言语是连续的物质信号，把它切分为一个个音素并不总是轻而易举。英语词 nab 与 wool 的波形图清楚地显示了这种差别：nab 的波形在三个明显不同的区域之间骤然过渡，而 wool 的波形自始至终平滑连贯，看不出明显的分界。本教材已为读者切分好词中的音素，但在处理一门陌生语言的原始录音时，音素之间的边界可能并不明确。"},{"en":"Once phones can be identified, they need a notation that conveys pronunciation unambiguously. Such a notation is a transcription, placed in square brackets, and it may be broad or narrow. An existing writing system cannot serve this purpose: English spelling uses the letter a for the vowels of nab, father, halo, and diva, while the same vowel in diva, meet, meat, me, and mummy can be written in different ways.","zh":"一旦能够辨认音素，就需要一种能无歧义地传达读音的标写方式。这种标写称为标音，写在方括号内，可宽可严。现成的书写系统无法胜任这一任务：英语拼写中字母 a 可表示 nab、father、halo、diva 中的不同元音，而 diva、meet、meat、me、mummy 中的同一元音又用不同的字母或字母组合表示。"},{"en":"The International Phonetic Alphabet was created by the International Phonetic Association, founded in 1886, and has been revised many times; its newest symbol, the labiodental tap [ⱱ], was added in 2005. The IPA's value lies less in memorizing symbols than in understanding the concepts behind them, much as the periodic table matters for what its entries mean rather than for the symbols alone.","zh":"国际音标由国际语音协会创制，该协会成立于 1886 年，此后这套标音系统历经多次修订，最新的一个符号是 2005 年增补的唇齿闪音 [ⱱ]。国际音标的价值不在于背下符号，而在于理解符号背后的概念，就像元素周期表的意义在于各项所代表的含义，而不只是符号本身。"},{"en":"When transcribing English, the IPA recommends the typographically simplest notation that still conveys the crucial information. English r varies enormously, from alveolar [ɹ] to retroflex [ɻ] and beyond, so a plain [r] is a reasonable broad choice. Likewise the affricate of chin is usually written [t͡ʃ] rather than the more accurate [ṯ͡ʃʷ], because the postalveolar release already implies a postalveolar closure.","zh":"在标写英语时，国际音标建议采用仍能传达关键信息的、排印上最简洁的写法。英语的 r 变体极多，从齿龈音 [ɹ] 到卷舌音 [ɻ] 等不一而足，因此宽式标音中选用普通的 [r] 是合理的。同样，chin 中的塞擦音通常写作 [t͡ʃ]，而不写更精确的 [ṯ͡ʃʷ]，因为龈后除阻本身已经蕴含了龈后的闭塞位置。"}]},"chapter-024-slug-3-7-signed-language-articulators":{"title":{"en":"3.7 Signed language articulators","zh":"3.7 手语发音器官"},"summary":{"en":"Signed languages have articulatory properties just as spoken ones do, but the units differ: a sign is a whole independent word, while the shape and the location of the hand cannot be separated from each other. The manual articulators are the arms, hands, and fingers, which move at six kinds of joints; the rest of the body forms the nonmanual articulators. The section shows how to identify which joints move in a sign.","zh":"手语和口语一样具有发音属性，但单位并不相同：一个手语符号本身就是独立的词，而手的形状与所在位置则彼此不可分离。手部发音器官是手臂、手和手指，它们通过六类关节运动；身体其余部分构成非手部发音器官。本节示范如何判断一个手语符号中哪些关节正在运动。"},"points":[{"en":"Signed languages have two units of articulation: whole signs and the individual articulatory properties of a sign.","zh":"手语的发音单位有两个层次：完整的手语符号，以及符号内部各项具体的发音属性。"},{"en":"Handshape and location are inseparable, just as place and manner of articulation cannot be chosen independently.","zh":"手的形状与位置不可分离，正如发音部位与发音方法也无法彼此独立地选定。"},{"en":"The manual articulators are the arms, hands, and fingers, moving at the shoulder, elbow, radioulnar, wrist, base knuckle, and interphalangeal joints.","zh":"手部发音器官包括手臂、手和手指，通过肩、肘、桡尺、腕、指根（掌指）和指间等六类关节运动。"},{"en":"The shoulder is very mobile; the elbow and interphalangeal joints mainly flex and extend; the wrist and base knuckles cannot rotate.","zh":"肩关节活动范围最大；肘和指间关节主要作屈伸运动；腕关节与指根关节则不能旋转。"},{"en":"Nonmanual articulators such as the torso, head, and face carry meaning, so hand-tracking gloves cannot translate signing fully.","zh":"躯干、头部和面部等非手部发音器官也承载意义，因此只追踪手部的翻译手套无法完整翻译手语。"}],"terms":[{"en":"manual articulators","zh":"手部发音器官","defEn":"The arms, hands, and fingers, which are the primary articulators used for signing.","defZh":"手臂、手和手指，是打手语时最主要使用的发音器官，也是手语发音研究的主要对象。"},{"en":"nonmanual articulators","zh":"非手部发音器官","defEn":"Body parts other than the hands that contribute to signing, such as the torso, head, and face.","defZh":"除手以外参与手语表达的身体部位，如躯干、头部和面部，也称非手部成分。"},{"en":"abduction","zh":"外展","defEn":"Movement of a limb outward or upward, away from the midline of the body.","defZh":"肢体向外或向上、离开身体中线的运动，如肩或腕的侧向抬离。"},{"en":"adduction","zh":"内收","defEn":"Movement of a limb inward or downward, towards the midline of the body.","defZh":"肢体向内或向下、朝向身体中线的运动，与「外展」方向相反。"},{"en":"flexion","zh":"屈曲","defEn":"Bending a joint so that the angle between the bones becomes smaller.","defZh":"弯曲关节，使相关两块骨头之间的夹角变小、肢体向身体收拢的运动。"},{"en":"extension","zh":"伸展","defEn":"Bending a joint in the opposite direction, straightening the bones involved.","defZh":"朝相反方向弯曲关节，使相关骨头伸直的运动，与「屈曲」相对。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[bɛd]","noteEn":"The English word bed, whose individual phones can each be pronounced on their own.","noteZh":"英语词 bed 的音标，其中每个音素都可以单独说出，说明音素具有独立性。"},{"text":"SORRY","noteEn":"An ASL sign with repeated elbow flexion and extension and repeated shoulder abduction and adduction.","noteZh":"一个美国手语符号，运动中包含肘的反复屈伸以及肩的反复外展和内收。"},{"text":"APPLE","noteEn":"An ASL sign whose only movement is repeated rotation of the radioulnar joint.","noteZh":"一个美国手语符号，其唯一运动来自桡尺关节的反复旋转。"},{"text":"CHOOSE","noteEn":"An ASL sign with non-repeated base knuckle flexion and wrist extension.","noteZh":"一个美国手语符号，包含一次性的指根关节屈曲与腕关节伸展。"}],"body":[{"en":"Signed languages lack a direct equivalent of the phone. A sign is the basic independent meaningful unit, comparable to a spoken word, but its articulatory properties, such as the shape of the hand and its location, cannot be separated: shaping the hand necessarily happens somewhere, and placing it somewhere necessarily involves configuring the fingers. Spoken languages thus have three units (words, articulatory properties, and phones), while signed languages clearly have two (signs and their articulatory properties); whether a third intermediate unit exists is debated.","zh":"手语没有与音素直接对应的单位。手语符号是基本的独立表意单位，大致相当于口语的词，但其各项发音属性彼此不可分离：手要以某种方式成形，必然是在某个位置上成形；要把手放到某个位置，也必然涉及手指的某种配置。因此口语有三类单位（词、发音属性、音素），而手语明确具有两类（手语符号及其发音属性）；是否存在居中的第三类单位，仍有争论。"},{"en":"The manual articulators are the arms, hands, and fingers, and they move by means of joints. Six joint types are distinguished: shoulder, elbow, radioulnar, wrist, base knuckles, and interphalangeal joints. The shoulder allows abduction and adduction, flexion and extension, and rotation, giving the upper arm a wide range of motion. The elbow is more restricted, mainly flexing and extending, and it cannot usually extend backwards from a hanging position. The radioulnar joint lets the radius and ulna pivot around each other, rotating the forearm.","zh":"手部发音器官是手臂、手和手指，它们依靠关节运动。这里区分六类关节：肩、肘、桡尺、腕、指根（掌指）和指间关节。肩关节可作外展与内收、屈曲与伸展以及旋转，使上臂具有很大的活动范围。肘关节活动较为受限，主要作屈伸，而且通常不能从下垂位置向后伸展。桡尺关节使桡骨与尺骨相互扭转，从而实现前臂的旋转。"},{"en":"The wrist and base knuckles allow abduction, adduction, extension, and flexion but no rotation, while the interphalangeal joints only flex and extend. When describing a sign, only the core movement counts; transitional movements into and out of the sign are ignored, as is any fixed configuration of joints. Analysing the ASL sign SORRY, for instance, leaves the elbow and shoulder as the joints of interest, since the hand traces a circle through repeated elbow flexion and extension together with shoulder abduction and adduction.","zh":"腕关节和指根关节可作外展、内收、伸展和屈曲，但不能旋转；指间关节只能屈伸。描写一个手语符号时，只有核心运动才算数：进入和退出手语符号的过渡动作被忽略，关节固定的配置也不算运动。例如分析美国手语符号 SORRY 时，真正相关的关节只剩下肘和肩，因为手在胸前画圈，动作包括肘的反复屈伸以及肩的外展和内收。"},{"en":"All remaining body parts are nonmanual articulators, especially the torso, head, and face, which produce gaze changes, eyebrow movements, head tilts, and lip shapes. These are part of a sign and cannot be ignored, which is one reason gloves that track only the hands cannot translate signed languages completely.","zh":"身体其余部分构成非手部发音器官，尤其是躯干、头部和面部，可产生目光变化、眉毛升降、头部倾斜、唇形变化等。这些动作是手语符号的组成部分，在完整的分析中不可忽略；这正是只追踪手部的翻译手套无法完整翻译手语的原因之一。"}]},"chapter-025-slug-3-8-describing-signs":{"title":{"en":"3.8 Describing signs","zh":"3.8 描写手语符号"},"summary":{"en":"Manual articulations fall into four parameters: handshape, orientation, location, and movement. Handshapes are often named after the numbers or letters they represent in a particular signed language, but those labels do not carry over between languages. Orientation splits into palm orientation and finger orientation, while movement divides into path movement at the elbow and shoulder and local movement at the other joints. Signs differing in one parameter form minimal pairs.","zh":"手部发音可归入四个参数：手形、朝向、位置和运动。手形常借用它在某一手语中代表的数字或字母来命名，但这些名称不能跨语言通用。朝向分为掌向与手指朝向；运动分为由肘和肩完成的路径运动与由其余关节完成的局部运动。只在一个参数上有差别的手语符号构成最小对立对。"},"points":[{"en":"Manual articulations are grouped into four parameters: handshape, orientation, location, and movement.","zh":"手部发音可归为四个参数：手形、朝向、位置和运动，它们是描写手语符号的基本维度。"},{"en":"Handshapes are often named after the letter or number they represent, but these names are not universal across signed languages.","zh":"手形常按它所代表的字母或数字命名，但这些名称在不同的手语之间并不通用。"},{"en":"Some handshapes are unmarked: the most common across languages, acquired earliest by children, and easiest to articulate and distinguish.","zh":"有些手形属于无标记手形：在各国手语中最常见、儿童最早习得，也最容易发出和区分。"},{"en":"Orientation has two components, palm orientation and finger orientation, and depends only on the wrist, radioulnar, elbow, and shoulder joints.","zh":"朝向包含掌向和手指朝向两个成分，只取决于腕、桡尺、肘和肩这四个关节。"},{"en":"Movement is path movement at the elbow or shoulder or local movement at the radioulnar, wrist, base knuckle, or interphalangeal joints.","zh":"运动分为路径运动与局部运动：前者由肘或肩完成，后者由桡尺、腕、指根或指间关节完成。"},{"en":"Signs that differ in only one parameter are minimal pairs, and a minimal pair can turn on any one of the four.","zh":"只在一个参数上有差别的手语符号构成最小对立对，四个参数中的任何一个都可以成为区别所在。"}],"terms":[{"en":"parameters","zh":"参数","defEn":"The four categories of manual articulation: handshape, orientation, location, and movement.","defZh":"对手部发音所作的四类划分，即手形、朝向、位置和运动，也称基本要素。"},{"en":"handshape","zh":"手形","defEn":"The static configuration of the base knuckles and interphalangeal joints in a sign.","defZh":"一个手语符号中指根关节与指间关节的静态配置方式，由各关节是否屈曲及程度决定。"},{"en":"orientation","zh":"朝向","defEn":"The direction the hand faces, determined by the wrist, radioulnar, elbow, and shoulder joints.","defZh":"手所面对的方向，由腕、桡尺、肘和肩四个关节的配置决定。"},{"en":"location","zh":"位置","defEn":"Where in space or on the body a sign is articulated.","defZh":"一个手语符号在空间中或身体上被发出的位置，默认位置是身前的中性手语空间。"},{"en":"movement","zh":"运动","defEn":"How the manual articulators move, divided into path movement and local movement.","defZh":"手部发音器官如何运动，分为在肘和肩完成的路径运动与在其余关节完成的局部运动。"},{"en":"minimal pair","zh":"最小对立对","defEn":"A pair of signs differing in just one parameter.","defZh":"只在一个参数上存在差别的一对手语符号，可用来确定该参数具有区别作用。"}],"examples":[{"text":"SORRY and PLEASE","noteEn":"An ASL minimal pair differing in handshape: open-A versus open-B.","noteZh":"美国手语中的最小对立对，二者的手形不同，分别为 open-A 与 open-B。"},{"text":"PROOF versus STOP","noteEn":"An ASL minimal pair differing in orientation, with the dominant palm up in PROOF and facing left in STOP.","noteZh":"美国手语中的最小对立对，区别在朝向：PROOF 的掌心向上，STOP 的掌心朝向说话人左侧。"},{"text":"APPLE versus ONION","noteEn":"An ASL minimal pair differing in location: the cheek versus the side of the head near the eye.","noteZh":"美国手语中的最小对立对，区别在位置：APPLE 在脸颊，ONION 在头部靠近眼睛的一侧。"},{"text":"THINK versus WONDER","noteEn":"An ASL minimal pair differing in movement: inward motion versus a circle near the head.","noteZh":"美国手语中的最小对立对，区别在运动：THINK 向头部移动，WONDER 在头部附近画圈。"}],"body":[{"en":"Many manual articulations recur in the same combinations, so they are grouped into four parameters, also called primes: handshape, orientation, location, and movement. Handshape is the static configuration of the base knuckles and interphalangeal joints, described by which joints are flexed and by how much. Because prose descriptions are cumbersome, handshapes are often drawn or labelled with the letter or number they represent.","zh":"许多手部发音方式反复以相同的组合出现，因此可以归入四个参数（也称基本要素）：手形、朝向、位置和运动。手形是指根关节与指间关节的静态配置，可根据哪些关节发生屈曲以及屈曲的程度来描写。由于文字描写相当累赘，手形常常直接用图形表示，或用它所代表的字母、数字来命名。"},{"en":"Those labels must be used cautiously. The S handshape represents the English letter in ASL but the Swedish letter G in Swedish Sign Language, and Russian Sign Language cannot be described with an R handshape at all, since its alphabet uses the Cyrillic letter Р, represented by the handshape that is EIGHT in ASL. Beyond letters and numbers, many handshapes have no such label. Some are unmarked, being the most common and earliest acquired, while marked handshapes are not universal and differ in frequency across languages.","zh":"使用这些名称时必须谨慎：S 手形在美国手语中代表英文字母，在瑞典手语中却代表瑞典语字母 G；俄语手语更无法用 R 手形来描述，因为其字母表使用西里尔字母 Р，而该字母在美国手语中对应的手形恰恰是 EIGHT。除字母和数字之外，许多手形并没有这类名称。部分手形是无标记的，最为常见，也最早被儿童习得；有标记手形则并不通用，在不同语言中的常见程度也不相同。"},{"en":"The other four joints produce orientation, which has a palm component and a finger component; bending the base knuckles changes handshape only. Location is where in space or on the body a sign is made, most often neutral signing space in front of the torso or some part of the head. Movement divides into path movement at the elbow or shoulder and local movement at the radioulnar, wrist, base knuckle, or interphalangeal joints, and it interacts with the other parameters.","zh":"其余四个关节决定朝向，朝向包含掌向与手指朝向两个成分；弯曲指根关节只会改变手形，不会改变朝向。位置是一个手语符号在空间中或身体上被发出的地方，最常见的是身前的中性手语空间或头部的某一部位。运动分为由肘或肩完成的路径运动与由桡尺、腕、指根或指间关节完成的局部运动，并与其他参数相互交织，因此分析一个手语符号时需要同时说明各参数的配合情况。"}]},"chapter-026-slug-3-9-signed-language-notation":{"title":{"en":"3.9 Signed language notation","zh":"3.9 手语标音法"},"summary":{"en":"There is no widely accepted equivalent of the IPA for transcribing signs. The most historically significant system, Stokoe notation, analyses each sign into location, handshape, orientation, and movement, and its underlying idea shaped later systems such as SignWriting and HamNoSys. Because no consistent standard has emerged, and special symbols are hard to display, describing signed language phonetics remains difficult.","zh":"目前没有像国际音标那样被普遍接受的手语转写系统。历史上最重要的斯托科标音法把每个手语词分析为位置、手形、掌向和运动四个参数，这一思路影响了后来的手语书写系统与汉堡标音系统。由于始终未形成统一标准，且专用符号难以显示，手语语音学与音系学的研究仍存在困难。"},"points":[{"en":"Stokoe's notation divides signs into parameters and helped establish the field of signed language linguistics.","zh":"斯托科标音法把词分解为若干参数，其研究也奠定了手语语言学这一领域。"},{"en":"A basic one-handed sign has the structure LHOM: location, handshape, subscript orientation, superscript movement.","zh":"单手基本词的记法结构为 LHOM，即位置、手形、下标掌向与上标运动。"},{"en":"Stokoe notation was designed for ASL, while SignWriting and HamNoSys use more iconic symbols.","zh":"斯托科标音法是为美国手语设计的，而手语书写与汉堡标音系统的符号更具象似性。"},{"en":"No consistent standard exists, and the special symbols are often unavailable in ordinary fonts.","zh":"至今没有统一标准，专用符号在普通字体中往往无法显示。"},{"en":"This lack of a standard notation makes signed language phonetics and phonology harder to study.","zh":"缺乏标准记音方式使手语语音学与音系学研究更加困难。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Stokoe notation","zh":"斯托科标音法","defEn":"A symbol system that analyses signs into location, handshape, orientation, and movement.","defZh":"由斯托科创制的符号系统，把词分析为位置、手形、掌向与运动四个参数。"},{"en":"handshape","zh":"手形","defEn":"One of the parameters of a sign, describing the shape of the hand.","defZh":"手语词的参数之一，指手部构型，即手指与手掌共同构成的形状。"},{"en":"palm orientation","zh":"掌向","defEn":"The parameter describing which way the palm faces during a sign.","defZh":"手语词的参数之一，描述发词时手掌朝向何方，如朝向说话者或背离说话者。"},{"en":"SignWriting","zh":"手语书写（SignWriting）","defEn":"A later notation system with iconic symbols that is not tied to ASL.","defZh":"较晚出现的标音系统，符号具象似性，且不依附于美国手语。"},{"en":"HamNoSys","zh":"汉堡标音系统（HamNoSys）","defEn":"The Hamburg Notation System, a later iconic notation not tied to ASL.","defZh":"汉堡标音系统的缩写，符号具象似性，不依附于美国手语。"},{"en":"nonmanual articulation","zh":"非手控发音","defEn":"Articulation of the face or body, sometimes treated as a fifth parameter.","defZh":"指面部或身体的动作，如表情与点头，有时被视为手语词四参数之外的第五个参数。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the ASL sign THANK-YOU","noteEn":"A basic sign whose Stokoe notation includes location, handshape, orientation, and movement.","noteZh":"一个基本词，其斯托科标音包含位置、手形、掌向与运动四个成分。"},{"text":"the B handshape with the thumb extended","noteEn":"In the example, the symbol B with a dot marks the handshape parameter.","noteZh":"在该例中，带点的符号 B 标示手形这一参数。"},{"text":"it is notated by U in Stokoe notation","noteEn":"The U handshape represents the English letter U in ASL, hence its Stokoe symbol.","noteZh":"U 手形在美国手语中表示英文字母 U，因此斯托科标音用 U 表示它。"},{"text":"the same handshape is used for the Arabic letter <ت> (Hendriks 2008), which represents the phone [t]","noteEn":"In Jordanian Sign Language the same handshape stands for a different letter.","noteZh":"在约旦手语中，同一手形表示的是另一个字母。"}],"body":[{"en":"Signs have no commonly accepted equivalent of the International Phonetic Alphabet. The most historically significant system was created by William Stokoe, whose work also demonstrated that signed languages have the same kinds of linguistic structures as spoken languages and thereby helped launch the field of signed language linguistics.","zh":"手语目前没有像国际音标那样被普遍接受的转写系统。历史上最重要的标音系统由斯托科（William Stokoe）创制；他的研究还证明手语具备与口语相同的语言结构，从而推动了手语语言学这一领域的诞生。"},{"en":"Stokoe notation divides signs according to the four parameters, treating orientation as a subcomponent of handshape, although Battison argued that orientation is a separate parameter, which is now the standard analysis; nonmanual articulations are sometimes counted as a fifth. A basic one-handed sign has the structure LHOM, with L for location, H for handshape, a subscript O for orientation, and a superscript M for movement, and further marks cover complex signs.","zh":"斯托科标音法按四个参数划分手语词，最初把掌向视为手形的下位成分；巴蒂森（Battison）主张掌向应独立为一个参数，这已成为标准的内部结构分析，非手控发音有时被算作第五个参数。单手基本词的结构为 LHOM：L 表示位置，H 表示手形，下标 O 表示掌向，上标 M 表示运动；更复杂的词可加用其他符号。"},{"en":"Because the system was designed for ASL, it does not serve signed languages generally, but its parametric approach influenced later systems such as SignWriting and HamNoSys, which use more iconic symbols and have no inherent ties to ASL. The U handshape, for instance, is notated by U in Stokoe notation because it represents the English letter U in ASL, yet the same handshape stands for the Arabic letter ت in Jordanian Sign Language.","zh":"由于该系统是为美国手语设计的，它并不适用于一般的手语；但其按参数分析的思路影响了后来的手语书写系统和汉堡标音系统，后两者的符号更具象似性，且不依附于美国手语。例如 U 手形在美国手语中表示英文字母 U，故在斯托科标音中记作 U；而在约旦手语中，同一手形表示阿拉伯字母 ت。"},{"en":"No single consistent standard has emerged. Existing systems typically need special symbols that most fonts do not contain, so many people cannot access them and documents may not display reliably on different computers. This makes the study of signed language phonetics and phonology more difficult.","zh":"至今没有形成统一的标准。现有系统通常需要大多数字体并不包含的专用符号，许多人无法获取这些符号，文档在不同电脑上也未必能可靠显示。这使手语语音学与音系学的研究更加困难。"}]},"chapter-027-slug-3-10-syllables":{"title":{"en":"3.10 Syllables","zh":"3.10 音节"},"summary":{"en":"Beyond individual phones, spoken words group into syllables, each built around a nucleus with optional onset and coda margins. Syllables may be shown in tree diagrams or abbreviated in CV-notation, and languages generally prefer onsets to codas and simple margins to complex ones. Syllabification often follows sonority, and signed languages may have comparable syllable-like units.","zh":"在单个音素之外，口语的词还组织成音节，每个音节以韵核为中心，两侧有可选的音节首和韵尾。音节结构可用树形图表示，也可用 CV 记法简写；跨语言来看，音节首比韵尾更受偏好，简单边缘比复杂边缘更受偏好。音节划分常以音响度为依据，手语中也可能存在类似的类音节单位。"},"points":[{"en":"Words divide into syllables, each with a nucleus and optional onset and coda margins.","zh":"词可划分为音节，每个音节有韵核以及可选的音节首和韵尾。"},{"en":"Syllable structure can be shown in a tree diagram or abbreviated in CV-notation.","zh":"音节结构可用树形图表示，也可用 CV 记法简写。"},{"en":"Across languages, onsets are preferred to codas, and simple margins to complex margins.","zh":"跨语言来看，音节首比韵尾更受偏好，简单边缘比复杂边缘更受偏好。"},{"en":"Syllabification is often based on sonority and usually obeys the sonority sequencing principle.","zh":"音节划分常以音响度为基础，通常遵循音响度序列原则。"},{"en":"Signs may also have syllable-like units, commonly analysed as static states and dynamic states.","zh":"手语词可能也有类音节单位，通常分析为静态单位与动态单位。"}],"terms":[{"en":"syllable","zh":"音节","defEn":"A unit of structure containing a nucleus and possibly onset and coda margins.","defZh":"一种结构单位，包含韵核以及可能出现的音节首和韵尾。"},{"en":"onset","zh":"音节首","defEn":"The margin to the left of the nucleus, either simple or complex.","defZh":"音节中位于韵核左侧的边缘成分，由辅音充当，可分为简单与复杂两类。"},{"en":"nucleus","zh":"韵核","defEn":"The loudest, most prominent position in a syllable, usually a vowel.","defZh":"音节中最响亮、最凸显的位置，通常由元音充当，也可由成音节辅音充当。"},{"en":"coda","zh":"韵尾","defEn":"The margin to the right of the nucleus, either simple or complex.","defZh":"音节中位于韵核右侧的边缘成分，由辅音充当，可分为简单与复杂两类。"},{"en":"sonority","zh":"音响度","defEn":"An abstract measure of the relative prominence of phones, roughly loudness.","defZh":"衡量音素相对凸显程度的抽象尺度，大致相当于响度，元音最高，阻塞音最低。"},{"en":"syllabification","zh":"音节划分","defEn":"The association of phones to appropriate positions in syllable structure.","defZh":"把各个音素指派到音节结构中相应位置的过程，通常以音响度为依据。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[kæ.nə.də] Canada","noteEn":"Syllable boundaries are marked with the IPA symbol [.] between syllables.","noteZh":"音节边界在转写中用国际音标符号 [.] 标示。"},{"text":"[ə.prot͡ʃ] approach","noteEn":"The first syllable has no margins; the second has a complex onset and simple coda.","noteZh":"其第一个音节没有边缘成分，第二个音节有复杂音节首和简单韵尾。"},{"text":"[plænt] plant","noteEn":"Well formed, since sonority rises through the onset and falls through the coda.","noteZh":"该音节合乎音响度序列原则：音响度在音节首上升，在韵尾下降。"},{"text":"[ɡvphrt͡skhvni] გვფრცქვნი ‘you (singular) are peeling us’","noteEn":"A Georgian word whose complex onset tolerates sonority reversals.","noteZh":"格鲁吉亚语词，其复杂音节首容许音响度的方向反转。"}],"body":[{"en":"Spoken words are not only strings of phones; they also group into units called syllables, each of which may contain several phones. A syllable is often written with the Greek letter sigma, and boundaries are marked in transcription with [.], as in [kæ.nə.də] Canada. The most prominent position, the nucleus, is usually a vowel, though English permits syllabic consonants in [br̩d] bird, and Tashlhiyt Berber even allows syllabic obstruents in words such as [ts̩.kr̩] ‘she did’.","zh":"口语的词不只是音素的串连，它们还组合成称作音节的单位，一个音节可以包含多个音素。音节常用希腊字母 σ 表示，转写时音节边界用 [.] 标示，如 [kæ.nə.də] Canada。音节中最凸显的位置是韵核，通常由元音充当；不过英语允许成音节辅音，如 [br̩d] bird，塔舍尔希特柏柏尔语甚至允许成音节阻塞音，如 [ts̩.kr̩]「她做了」。"},{"en":"The remaining phones form the margins: the onset on the left and the coda on the right, each either simple or complex. In [ə.prot͡ʃ] approach, the first syllable has no onset or coda while the second has a complex onset [pr] and a simple coda [t͡ʃ]; affricates count as one phone in margins, but diphthongs usually count as two. Syllable structure may be drawn as a tree diagram or abbreviated in CV-notation, so [ə.prot͡ʃ] becomes V.CCVC. A syllable without a coda is open, one with a coda is closed, and one without an onset is onsetless.","zh":"其余音素构成边缘成分：左侧为音节首，右侧为韵尾，二者都可分为简单与复杂两类。在 [ə.prot͡ʃ] approach 中，第一个音节没有音节首和韵尾，第二个音节有复杂音节首 [pr] 和简单韵尾 [t͡ʃ]；塞擦音在边缘中算作一个音素，而复元音通常算作两个。音节结构可画成树形图，也可用 CV 记法简写，因此 [ə.prot͡ʃ] 可记作 V.CCVC。没有韵尾的音节是开音节，有韵尾的是闭音节，没有音节首的则称无首音节。"},{"en":"Across languages, onsets are preferred and codas disfavoured: languages may require onsets or prohibit codas, but not the reverse, and simple margins are preferred to complex ones. Languages also arrange sonority, the abstract prominence of phones, differently, yet syllabification usually obeys the sonority sequencing principle, which requires sonority to rise through the onset, peak in the nucleus, and fall through the coda. Thus [plænt] plant is well formed, while *[lpætn] violates the principle.","zh":"跨语言来看，音节首受偏好而韵尾不受偏好：语言可能要求有音节首或禁止韵尾，却不会有相反的情况，简单边缘也比复杂边缘更受偏好。各语言对音响度这一抽象凸显程度的排列可以不同，但音节划分通常遵循音响度序列原则，即音响度在音节首上升、在韵核达到顶点、在韵尾下降。因此 [plænt] plant 是合格的音节，而 *[lpætn] 违反该原则。"},{"en":"Syllables also have a somewhat questionable status, since speakers' intuitions about hire [haɪr] and higher [haɪ.r̩] often do not match their own recorded speech, which suggests syllables have psychological rather than physical reality. Signed languages may likewise have syllable-like units, commonly analysed as sequences of static states, roughly location plus orientation, and dynamic states, essentially movement, with dynamic units claimed to be more sonorous. Whether a syllabic model truly applies to signed languages remains an open question.","zh":"音节的地位也因此有些可疑：说话人对 hire [haɪr] 与 higher [haɪ.r̩] 的直觉往往与他们自己录音中的发音并不吻合，这说明音节可能只具有心理现实性，而非物理现实性。手语中可能同样存在类音节单位，通常分析为静态单位（大致相当于位置加掌向）与动态单位（基本上即运动）的序列，并有人认为动态单位音响度更高。音节模型是否真正适用于手语，仍是一个开放问题。"}]},"chapter-028-slug-3-11-stress":{"title":{"en":"3.11 Stress","zh":"3.11 重音"},"summary":{"en":"Stressed syllables are made prominent through greater loudness, longer duration, or higher pitch in speech, and through tension or longer holds in signs. Most words have exactly one primary stress, while other stressed syllables carry secondary stress. Stress may be lexical and therefore unpredictable, or fully predictable from syllable structure, subject to a small set of restrictions.","zh":"在口语中，重读音节通过更强的响度、更长的时长或更高的音高获得凸显；手语则以更强的肌肉紧张或更长的保持动作实现类似效果。多数词只有一个主重音，其余重读音节为次重音。重音既可能是需要逐词记忆、因而不可预测的词汇性重音，也可能完全由音节结构预测，并受到少数几条限制的约束。"},"points":[{"en":"Stressed syllables are prominent through loudness, duration, or pitch; signed languages use tension and holds.","zh":"重读音节靠响度、时长或音高凸显；手语则通过肌肉紧张和保持动作实现。"},{"en":"Primary stress is marked [ˈ] and secondary stress [ˌ] before the onset of a syllable.","zh":"主重音在音节首之前用 [ˈ] 标记，次重音用 [ˌ] 标记。"},{"en":"Lexical stress is unpredictable and can create minimal pairs, as in Khowar.","zh":"词汇性重音不可预测，可形成最小对立对，如霍瓦语中的例子。"},{"en":"Predictable stress usually falls on one of the first two or last two syllables.","zh":"可预测的重音通常落在词的前两个或后两个音节之一上。"},{"en":"Secondary stress tends to alternate, and not all imaginable stress patterns occur.","zh":"次重音往往交替出现，而并非所有可想象的重音模式都存在。"}],"terms":[{"en":"stress","zh":"重音","defEn":"The prominence given to a syllable within the linguistic signal.","defZh":"音节在语言信号中所获得的凸显，由响度、时长、音高等语音属性共同实现。"},{"en":"primary stress","zh":"主重音","defEn":"The single highest degree of stress within a word.","defZh":"一个词中程度最高的那一个重音，通常每词只有一个，在音节首之前用 [ˈ] 标记。"},{"en":"secondary stress","zh":"次重音","defEn":"Stress lower than primary, marked with a lower tick mark.","defZh":"程度低于主重音的重音，在音节首之前用低竖线符号 [ˌ] 标记。"},{"en":"lexical stress","zh":"词汇性重音","defEn":"Stress whose placement is unpredictable and memorized for each word.","defZh":"位置不可预测、需要逐词记忆的重音，可形成最小对立对。"},{"en":"penultimate stress","zh":"倒数第二音节重音","defEn":"Primary stress on the second syllable from the end of a word.","defZh":"主重音落在词的倒数第二个音节上的重音模式，是常见的可预测模式之一。"},{"en":"stress-timed","zh":"重音计时（stress-timed）","defEn":"A rejected classification in which stresses fall at roughly equal intervals.","defZh":"一种已被否定的分类，认为重音之间时间间隔大致相等。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[ˈbʌ.niˌhʌɡ] bunny hug","noteEn":"A Saskatchewan English word for a hoodie, showing all three degrees of stress.","noteZh":"萨斯喀彻温英语中表示连帽衫的词，展示三个重音等级。"},{"text":"[ˈtɑɾu] ‘fast runner’ versus [tɑˈɾu] ‘batter’","noteEn":"A Khowar minimal pair distinguished only by the placement of stress.","noteZh":"霍瓦语的最小对立对，仅靠重音位置区分意义。"},{"text":"[ˈklinˈʃevn̩] clean-shaven","noteEn":"A compound in which two syllables carry roughly equal primary stress.","noteZh":"复合词，其中两个音节带有大致相等的主重音。"},{"text":"I’m going to the store to buy milk and eggs","noteEn":"Sentence in which the preposition to and the conjunction and are unstressed.","noteZh":"句中前置词 to 与连词 and 通常不重读。"}],"body":[{"en":"As organising units, syllables shape the rhythm of language, especially because stressed syllables are more prominent in the linguistic signal. In speech, stressed syllables often combine increased loudness, longer duration, and higher pitch; signed languages with syllables seem to mark stress with greater muscular tension, quicker movements, or longer holds. Languages differ considerably in which phonetic properties they use. The common stress-timed versus syllable-timed classification, however, lacks phonetic support and is best avoided.","zh":"作为组织单位，音节塑造了语言的节奏，一个重要原因在于重读音节在语言信号中更为凸显。在口语中，重读音节往往兼有更强的响度、更长的时长和更高的音高；有音节的手语似乎以更强的肌肉紧张、更快的运动或更长的保持动作来标记重音。各语言使用哪些语音属性差异很大。不过，重音计时与音节计时这一通行分类缺乏语音事实的支持，最好避免使用。"},{"en":"In spoken languages a word may have many syllables and thus several degrees of stress. Usually exactly one syllable carries the highest degree, called primary stress and marked [ˈ] before the syllable onset; other stressed syllables have secondary stress, marked [ˌ] before the onset, and the remaining syllables are unstressed. All three levels appear in [ˈbʌ.niˌhʌɡ] bunny hug, a Saskatchewan English word for a hoodie. Non-IPA diacritics such as the acute and grave accents are also used, but must be applied carefully because they have other functions.","zh":"在口语中，一个词可以有多个音节，从而具备多个重音等级。通常恰有一个音节承载最高等级的重音，称为主重音，在音节首之前用 [ˈ] 标记；其他重读音节为次重音，在音节首之前用 [ˌ] 标记，其余音节不重读。三个等级都出现在 [ˈbʌ.niˌhʌɡ] bunny hug 中，这是萨斯喀彻温英语里表示连帽衫的说法。人们也用尖音符、抑音符等非国际音标符号标注重音，但这些符号另有用途，必须谨慎使用以免歧义。"},{"en":"Many languages have lexical stress, whose placement is unpredictable and must be memorized for each word, and this can create minimal pairs such as [ˈtɑɾu] ‘fast runner’ versus [tɑˈɾu] ‘batter’ in Khowar. In other languages stress is fully predictable from syllable structure. Predictable stress falls nearly always on one of the first two or the last two syllables, giving initial, peninitial, ultimate, and penultimate stress; antepenultimate stress also occurs, as if the final syllable were invisible, but a matching third-from-the-beginning pattern is not found.","zh":"许多语言具有词汇性重音，其位置不可预测，必须逐词记忆，这能形成最小对立对，如霍瓦语中 [ˈtɑɾu]「跑得快的人」与 [tɑˈɾu]「击球手」。在另一些语言中，重音完全可由音节结构预测。可预测的重音几乎总是落在词的前两个或后两个音节之一上，由此有首音节重音、第二音节重音、末音节重音和倒数第二音节重音；也会出现倒数第三音节重音，仿佛末音节不可见，却找不到与之对应的、从词首数第三个音节固定重音的模式。次重音往往每隔一个音节交替出现。"},{"en":"Despite such complexity, some generalisations hold. No spoken language consistently places primary stress on, say, the middle syllable of every word, nor does one consistently alternate two stressed with two unstressed syllables. This suggests deeper principles behind stress assignment, perhaps tied to its purpose: stress may aid processing, so it should be relatively regular and anchored to word boundaries. Not every imaginable stress pattern is possible; instead, a small set of specific restrictions seems to govern it.","zh":"尽管存在这些复杂性，仍有若干概括成立。没有哪种口语总是把主重音落在每个词的中间音节上，也没有哪种口语总是以两个重读音节与两个非重读音节交替。这说明重音的指派背后有更深层的原则，或许与重音的功能有关：重音可能有助于语言信号的加工，因此应相对规则，并锚定在词的边界上。并非所有可想象的重音模式都可行，支配重音的似乎只是少数几条具体限制。"}]},"chapter-029-slug-3-12-tone-and-intonation":{"title":{"en":"3.12 Tone and intonation","zh":"3.12 声调与语调"},"summary":{"en":"Spoken languages can manipulate pitch in two main ways. Tone contrasts syllables or whole words to produce different meanings, while intonation operates over phrases and sentences to signal conversational functions such as statements versus questions. The section explains how pitch is measured, surveys the three tone notation systems, and describes level, contour, and sentence-level pitch patterns.","zh":"口语语言对音高的运用主要有两种方式。声调作用于音节或整个词，用以区分不同的意义；语调则作用于短语和句子，表达陈述与疑问等交际功能。本节说明音高的物理与感知基础，介绍三种标调系统，并描述平调、曲拱声调以及句子层面的音高模式。"},"points":[{"en":"Pitch is our auditory perception of how fast the vocal folds vibrate; the physical measure is fundamental frequency (f0).","zh":"音高是人对声带振动快慢的听觉感知，其物理量度是基频（f0）。"},{"en":"Tone works at the syllable or word level, whereas intonation works over phrases and sentences to express conversational function.","zh":"声调作用于音节或词的层面，语调则作用于短语和句子，表达交际功能。"},{"en":"The IPA notates tone with diacritics above the phone or tone letters after the syllable, and non-IPA tone numbers are also common.","zh":"国际音标用音素上方的附加符号或音节后的调符标记声调，非国际音标的数字标调法也很常见。"},{"en":"Besides high, low, and mid level tones, languages may have contour tones that rise or fall within a single syllable.","zh":"除高、低、中平调之外，语言还可能具有在一个音节内上升或下降的曲拱声调。"},{"en":"Each notation system has drawbacks, including clashes with other traditions and limited font support for tone letters.","zh":"每种记音系统都有缺陷，或与其他标调传统冲突，或因字体支持不足而难以显示调符。"}],"terms":[{"en":"pitch","zh":"音高","defEn":"The auditory perception of the rate at which the vocal folds vibrate.","defZh":"对声带振动快慢的听觉感知，振动越快则音高越高。"},{"en":"tone","zh":"声调","defEn":"Pitch manipulated at the syllable or word level to make different meanings.","defZh":"在音节或词的层面运用音高，从而区分不同意义。"},{"en":"intonation","zh":"语调","defEn":"Pitch manipulated over phrases and sentences to convey conversational functions.","defZh":"在短语和句子层面运用音高，用以表达陈述、疑问等交际功能。"},{"en":"level tone","zh":"平调","defEn":"A tone whose pitch stays relatively stable from beginning to end.","defZh":"音高从起点到终点保持相对稳定的声调，如高平调与低平调。"},{"en":"contour tone","zh":"曲拱声调","defEn":"A tone that changes in pitch during the course of the syllable.","defZh":"在一个音节内部音高发生变化的声调，如降调与升调。"},{"en":"minimal triplet","zh":"最小三连对","defEn":"Three words that differ only in the tones of their syllables.","defZh":"三个词在音段上相同，仅靠声调形成对立的一组词。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[lúk] ‘vomit’ and [lùk] ‘weave’","noteEn":"Bemba one-syllable words differing only in high versus low tone.","noteZh":"本巴语的单音节词，仅以高调与低调形成对立。"},{"text":"[àwó] ‘slap’, [àwō] ‘comb’, [àwò] ‘star’","noteEn":"Igala minimal triplets with high, mid, and low second-syllable tones.","noteZh":"伊加拉语的最小三连对，第二音节分别为高调、中调、低调。"},{"text":"[nâ] ‘taro’ and [pǎ] ‘fish’","noteEn":"Awa falling and rising contour tones on a single syllable.","noteZh":"阿瓦语的降调与升调，都落在同一个音节上。"},{"text":"This is VEGETARIAN chili (not BEEF chili).","noteEn":"An English intonation pattern marking emphasis to correct a wrong assumption.","noteZh":"英语语调模式之一，通过强调某词来纠正对方的错误预设。"}],"body":[{"en":"During voicing the vocal folds vibrate at a certain rate. Linguists call that physical vibration fundamental frequency, abbreviated f0, and reserve the word pitch for our auditory perception of it. Since this discussion concerns abstract cognitive categories rather than speaker-specific physical details, the term pitch is used throughout. Pitch can also be manipulated as a system of its own.","zh":"发声时声带以一定频率振动。语言学家把这一物理振动称为基频，缩写为 f0，而把音高（pitch）留给对这一振动的听觉感知。由于本节关注的是抽象的认知范畴，而非因人而异的个人发音细节，因此全篇采用音高这一术语。音高在重音系统中还与时长、强度相互作用，但它也可以被单独调动，构成独立的系统。"},{"en":"When pitch is manipulated at the level of syllables or whole words to make completely different meanings, the system is called tone; when it operates over phrases and sentences to express conversational functions such as statements versus questions, it is called intonation. Languages are correspondingly described as tonal and intonational. Tone is notated in the IPA either with diacritics above the phone or with tone letters after the syllable, and non-IPA superscript numbers on a 1–5 scale are also common, as in Bemba [lúk] ‘vomit’ and [lùk] ‘weave’. Each system has drawbacks, including clashes with other numbering traditions and limited font support for tone letters.","zh":"若在音节或整个词的层面调动音高以产生完全不同的意义，这一系统称为声调；若在短语和句子层面调动音高，用以表达陈述或疑问等交际功能，则称为语调。语言也相应地分为声调语言和语调语言。国际音标或用音素上方的附加符号标调，或用音节后的调符标调，非国际音标的 1–5 上标数字也很常见，如本巴语的 [lúk]‘呕吐’与 [lùk]‘编织’。各系统均有缺陷：数字标调与威妥玛拼音 ma1 等传统冲突，附加符号与汉语拼音及重音标记重叠，调符则因字体支持不足而难以普遍显示。"},{"en":"In many tone languages each syllable can in principle carry its own tone, allowing a wide range of combinations, as in Bemba [βúːlá] ‘take’ and [ùkúwà] ‘fall’. Tone systems are not always binary: Igala has a mid tone between high and low, written with the macron [ˉ], the tone letter [˧], or the number [3], which yields minimal triplets such as [àwó] ‘slap’, [àwō] ‘comb’, and [àwò] ‘star’. Level tones hold a steady pitch, whereas contour tones change pitch within the syllable: Awa has falling [nâ] ‘taro’ and rising [pǎ] ‘fish’.","zh":"在许多声调语言中，每个音节原则上都可带有独立的声调，因而出现大量组合，如本巴语的 [βúːlá]‘拿取’与 [ùkúwà]‘落下’。声调系统并不总是二分的：伊加拉语有介于高低之间的中调，可用长音符号 [ˉ]、调符 [˧] 或数字 [3] 表示，由此形成 [àwó]‘拍打’、[àwō]‘梳子’、[àwò]‘星星’这样的最小三连对。平调音高保持稳定，曲拱声调则在音节内部改变音高：阿瓦语有降调 [nâ]‘芋头’和升调 [pǎ]‘鱼’。"},{"en":"Finally, pitch changes across whole sentences count as intonation, which conveys a sentence's function rather than which words it contains. The English sentence this is vegetarian chili takes many patterns depending on whether it is a statement or a question and on which word is emphasized, as in This is VEGETARIAN chili (not BEEF chili). Analysing intonation therefore draws on syntax, semantics, and pragmatics alike.","zh":"最后，贯穿整个句子的音高变化属于语调，它传达的是句子的功能，而非句子由哪些词构成。英语句子 this is vegetarian chili 可有许多语调模式，取决于它用作陈述句还是疑问句，以及强调的是哪个词，如 This is VEGETARIAN chili (not BEEF chili)。完整的语调分析需要兼顾句法、语义、语用以及词层面的重音或声调。"}]},"part-004-chapter-4-phonology":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 4: Phonology","zh":"第 4 章：音系学"},"summary":{"en":"The physical units of a linguistic signal are not combined randomly. Chapter 4 examines the abstract structure behind those patterns: how units may be combined, how neighbouring units affect one another's articulation, and how linguists discover such regularities within a language and across languages.","zh":"语言信号的物理单位并非随机组合。反复出现的模式与范畴，为这些物理现实赋予了抽象层次。本章考察这些组合模式背后的抽象结构：单位可以怎样组合、相邻单位在发音上如何互相影响，以及语言学家通过哪些方法去发现单一语言内部与跨语言的规律。"},"points":[{"en":"Repeated patterns and categories give abstract structure to the physical signal within and across languages.","zh":"反复出现的模式与范畴，为单一语言内部及跨语言的物理信号赋予抽象结构。"},{"en":"Learners should be able to determine the distributions of phones in a spoken language.","zh":"学习者应能够判定某一口语中各个音素所出现的分布情况。"},{"en":"Learners should be able to describe phonological processes in signed languages as well.","zh":"学习者也应能够描述手语中相应的音系过程与音系变化。"},{"en":"Phones are grouped into phonemes on the basis of their distributions.","zh":"音素依据它们出现的位置与分布被归并成为不同的音位。"},{"en":"Phonological rules map phonemes and underlying representations to allophones and surface representations.","zh":"音系规则把音位与底层形式映射为音位变体与表层形式。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonology","zh":"音系学","defEn":"the study of patterns in how the physical units of language combine","defZh":"研究一种语言中语音单位如何组合、如何相互影响的一门学科。"},{"en":"phone","zh":"音素","defEn":"a physical unit of the linguistic signal that can be measured directly","defZh":"语言信号中可以观察与测量的最小物理语音单位，如 [m]。"},{"en":"phoneme","zh":"音位","defEn":"an abstract unit whose physical realizations are treated as the same object","defZh":"抽象单位，其各种物理实现被说话者视为同一个音系对象。"},{"en":"underlying representation","zh":"底层形式","defEn":"the abstract form of a morpheme before phonological rules apply","defZh":"音系规则尚未作用之前，语素所具有的抽象的音系形式。"},{"en":"surface representation","zh":"表层形式","defEn":"the form actually produced after phonological rules have applied","defZh":"音系规则作用之后，实际说出的语音形式，也称语音输出。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"The phonetic properties of a language are not entirely random. Many repeated patterns and categories give additional abstract structure to the physical reality of the linguistic signal, and these regularities appear both inside a single language and across languages. This chapter investigates that structure by asking how the physical units of language may be combined, how they influence one another when they stand next to each other, and which methods linguists use to uncover such patterns.","zh":"语言的语音属性并非完全随机。许多反复出现的模式与范畴，为语言信号的物理现实增添了抽象结构，这些规律既存在于单一语言内部，也见于跨语言的比较。本章即考察这一结构：语言的物理单位可以怎样组合、它们相邻时如何相互影响，以及语言学家借助哪些方法来发现这些模式。"},{"en":"By the end of the chapter, students should be able to analyze linguistic data in order to determine the distributions of phones in a spoken language and the phonological processes of signed languages. They should also be able to categorize phones into phonemes according to those distributions, and to write phonological rules that show how phonemes and underlying representations map onto allophones and surface representations.","zh":"学完本章，学生应能分析语言材料，判定某一口语中音素的分布，并识别手语中的音系过程；还应能依据分布把音素归并为音位，并写出音系规则，说明音位与底层形式如何映射为音位变体与表层形式。"}]},"chapter-030-slug-4-1-phonemes-and-allophones":{"title":{"en":"4.1 Phonemes and allophones","zh":"4.1 音位与音位变体"},"summary":{"en":"Speakers treat certain physically different phones as the same abstract object. Such an object is a phoneme, and its concrete realizations are its allophones, each used in particular environments. Using English /t/ and the ASL sign HOME, the section shows how linguists infer phonemes from patterns of distribution rather than observing them directly.","zh":"说话者会把某些物理上不同的音素视为同一个抽象对象。这一对象就是音位，其具体实现即音位变体，各自出现在特定环境之中。本节以英语 /t/ 和美国手语符号 HOME 为例，说明音位无法被直接测量，语言学家只能从音素出现的分布模式中推断音位及其音位变体，并不断检验自己的推测。"},"points":[{"en":"The three phones [m], [i], and [k] form [mik] meek, but only [kim] of the other five orders could enter English.","zh":"音素 [m]、[i]、[k] 组成 [mik]，其余五种排列中只有 [kim] 能进入英语。"},{"en":"ASL HOME blends parameters of FOOD and BED rather than sequencing the two signs.","zh":"美国手语 HOME 融合了 FOOD 与 BED 的要素，而非把两个手语符号简单连缀。"},{"en":"Atom and atomic show the flap [ɾ] and the aspirated [tʰ] as allophones of the same phoneme.","zh":"atom 与 atomic 中的闪音 [ɾ] 与送气音 [tʰ] 是同一音位的两个音位变体。"},{"en":"The flap appears before an unstressed vowel or syllabic consonant, the aspirated stop before a stressed one.","zh":"闪音出现在非重读元音或成音节辅音之前，送气塞音则出现在重读元音之前。"},{"en":"Phonemes are abstractions that linguists infer from distribution, and analyses may differ across frameworks.","zh":"音位是语言学家从分布推断出的抽象单位，不同理论框架可能得出不同分析。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phoneme","zh":"音位","defEn":"an abstract set of allophones that speakers treat as one object","defZh":"抽象单位，其各种物理实现被说话者视为同一个音系对象。"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"one of the physical realizations of a phoneme in a specific environment","defZh":"某个音位在特定语音环境中所实现的一种具体语音形式。"},{"en":"environment","zh":"环境","defEn":"the phonetic context to the left, right, or both, that selects an allophone","defZh":"决定选用哪个音位变体的左侧、右侧或两侧相邻语音语境。"},{"en":"aspiration","zh":"送气","defEn":"a puff of air that follows a released voiceless plosive","defZh":"清塞音除阻之后随之呼出的一股气流，如 [tʰ] 中的 [ʰ]。"},{"en":"alveolar flap","zh":"齿龈闪音","defEn":"a rapid tongue-tip contact symbolized [ɾ] in the IPA","defZh":"舌尖快速拍击齿龈一次所发出的辅音，国际音标记作 [ɾ]。"},{"en":"modality","zh":"模态","defEn":"the channel of a language, spoken or signed, which shapes its phonology","defZh":"语言的口语或手语通道，它决定该语言音系的基本单位。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[mik] meek, [kim]","noteEn":"Only one of the six orderings of [m], [i], [k] could easily become an English word.","noteZh":"[m]、[i]、[k] 六种排列中，只有 [kim] 有可能轻松作为新词进入英语。"},{"text":"[ˈmɛɾl̩] metal and [məˈtʰælək] metallic, [ˈbæɾl̩] battle and [bəˈtʰæljn̩] battalion","noteEn":"Flap before unstressed vowel and aspirated stop before stressed vowel recur in these related pairs.","noteZh":"这些相关词对中反复出现非重读元音前用闪音、重读元音前用送气塞音的模式。"},{"text":"[ˈkrɪɾək] critic and [kraɪˈtʰiriə] criteria","noteEn":"Another related pair confirming the stress-based pattern for the phoneme /t/.","noteZh":"另一对相关词，同样印证 /t/ 受重音制约的模式。"},{"text":"FOOD and BED compound to form the sign HOME","noteEn":"The two signs merge, keeping the flat-O handshape and the location at the side of the face.","noteZh":"两个手语符号合并为 HOME，保留 flat-O 手形以及面部侧面的位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"A linguistic signal consists of small physical units such as phones, handshapes, and movements that are not strung together at random. Four of the six orderings of [m], [i], and [k] are normally unpronounceable for English speakers, while [kim] could readily be adopted as a new English word. Units also influence each other when combined: in American Sign Language, FOOD and BED merge into the single sign HOME rather than forming a sequence.","zh":"语言信号由音素、手形、运动等小型物理单位构成，这些单位并非随意串接。[m]、[i]、[k] 的六种排列中有四种通常为英语母语者所无法发音，而 [kim] 本可顺利成为新的英语词。单位相邻时还会互相影响：在美国手语中，FOOD 与 BED 合成 HOME，它保留 FOOD 的 flat-O 手形，位置则取自 BED 的面部侧面。"},{"en":"In spoken language, certain phones are pronounced differently, yet speakers treat them as one conceptual object. The consonant in atom is an alveolar flap [ɾ], while in atomic it is a voiceless alveolar plosive with a puff of air, [tʰ]. Because the words are related in sound and meaning, the two phones can be regarded as one object on an abstract level. That object is a phoneme, its various realizations are allophones, each used in particular environments, and the phoneme is written as /t/.","zh":"在口语中，某些音素发音不同，却仍被说话者视为同一个概念对象。atom 中间的辅音是齿龈闪音 [ɾ]，atomic 中对应的音素则是清齿龈塞音后接气流，即 [tʰ]。两个词在读音与意义上都明显相关，因此不妨在抽象层面把它们视为同一对象。这一对象就是音位，其各种实现即音位变体，各自与特定环境相系；按惯例音位写作斜线内的单一符号，此处即 /t/。音位不等于任何一次具体发音，而是一个由若干音位变体构成的抽象集合。"},{"en":"Allophonic environments involve phonetic properties immediately to the left, to the right, or both. Both allophones of /t/ occur between two vowels or syllabic consonants, but the flap requires an unstressed syllable to follow, the aspirated stop a stressed one. The conjecture holds for [ˈmɛɾl̩] metal and [məˈtʰælək] metallic, and beyond related pairs: data, writer, and Ottawa have [ɾ], while attack, return, and Saskatoon have [tʰ]. Stress thus decides the allophone.","zh":"音位变体的环境涉及紧邻左侧、右侧或两侧兼有的语音属性。/t/ 的两个变体都出现在两个元音或成音节辅音之间，但闪音之后须为非重读元音或成音节辅音，送气塞音之后则须为重读元音。这一推测在 [ˈmɛɾl̩] metal 与 [məˈtʰælək] metallic 中成立，且不限于相关词对：data、writer、Ottawa 用 [ɾ]，attack、return、Saskatoon 用 [tʰ]。可见重音决定音位变体的选择。"},{"en":"Linguists have no direct access to phonemes, which are abstractions rather than measurable reality; they must infer from where phones occur whether those phones belong together as allophones of one phoneme. Phonology therefore aims to establish a language's phonemes, their allophones, and each allophone's environment, and to seek universal principles of human language. Because modality matters greatly, spoken and signed phonology are best treated separately, and since phonological units are theoretical constructs, analyses may vary.","zh":"语言学家无法直接接触音位，它是抽象单位而非可测量的实体，研究者只能依据音素出现的位置来推断它们是否属于同一音位的音位变体。音系学的目标因此是确定一种语言的音位、各音位的音位变体及其环境，并探寻人类语言的普遍原则。由于模态影响甚大，口语音系学与手语音系学宜分开考察；又因音系单位是理论构念，不同语言学家与理论框架可能得出不同分析。"}]},"chapter-031-slug-4-2-phonotactics-and-natural-classes":{"title":{"en":"4.2 Phonotactics and natural classes","zh":"4.2 音位配列与自然类"},"summary":{"en":"Beyond changing in particular environments, physical units may be barred from certain positions altogether. Each language has its own phonotactics, and the sounds affected often form a natural class, a set of phones sharing phonetic properties and phonological behaviour. Natural classes are language-specific, as English and Kalaallisut show.","zh":"除了在特定环境中发生变化，物理单位还可能完全不能出现在某些位置上。每种语言都有自己的音位配列，而受同一限制的音往往构成自然类，即共享语音属性与音系行为的音素集合。自然类的成员因语言而异：英语中以清塞音为一类，格陵兰语中则必须把 [q] 也包括进来。"},"points":[{"en":"Phonotactics are language-specific restrictions on which combinations of units are allowed in which environments.","zh":"音位配列是语言特有的限制，规定哪些单位组合可以出现在哪些环境中。"},{"en":"English bans [tl] and [dl] in onsets, but Ngizim and Hebrew permit them.","zh":"英语禁止 [tl] 和 [dl] 作音节首，而恩吉齐姆语与希伯来语允许。"},{"en":"Some restrictions are loose: English speakers readily pronounce pueblo [pwɛblo] and Vladimir [vlædəmir].","zh":"有些限制较宽松：英语母语者仍能读出 pueblo 与 Vladimir 这样的词。"},{"en":"The ASL Symmetry Condition requires two-handed moving signs to share handshape and movement.","zh":"美国手语的对称条件要求双手运动的手语符号在手形与运动方式上一致。"},{"en":"A natural class is a set of phones sharing phonetic properties and phonological behaviour.","zh":"自然类指共享某些语音属性与音系行为的一组音素集合。"},{"en":"Natural classes are language-specific and must be exhaustive, as [q] in Kalaallisut shows.","zh":"自然类是语言特有的且必须穷尽，格陵兰语的 [q] 即可说明。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonotactics","zh":"音位配列（语音组合法）","defEn":"language-specific restrictions on which combinations of units may occur where","defZh":"某一语言对语音单位组合可出现在何种位置所作的特殊限制。"},{"en":"distribution","zh":"分布","defEn":"the overall pattern of environments in which a unit can occur","defZh":"某个语音单位能够出现的全部环境所构成的一种整体模式。"},{"en":"natural class","zh":"自然类","defEn":"a set of phones sharing phonetic properties and phonological behaviour","defZh":"共享某些语音属性并表现相同音系行为的一组音素集合。"},{"en":"onset","zh":"音节首","defEn":"the consonant or consonants that precede the nucleus of a syllable","defZh":"音节中位于韵核之前的那一个辅音或者多个辅音的组合。"},{"en":"Symmetry Condition","zh":"对称条件","defEn":"an ASL restriction requiring two moving hands to share handshape and movement","defZh":"美国手语的限制：双手同时运动时须手形与运动方式相同。"},{"en":"loanword","zh":"借词","defEn":"a word borrowed from another language into the vocabulary of a language","defZh":"从其他语言借入并被纳入本语言词汇系统之中的词语形式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[tlà] ‘cow’","noteEn":"A Ngizim word showing that [tl] onsets are permitted in that language.","noteZh":"恩吉齐姆语的词，说明该语言允许 [tl] 作音节首。"},{"text":"[dli] ‘bucket’","noteEn":"A Hebrew word with a [dl] onset, which English phonotactics would ban.","noteZh":"希伯来语的词，其 [dl] 音节首为英语音位配列所禁止。"},{"text":"pueblo [pwɛblo] and Vladimir [vlædəmir]","noteEn":"Loanword and proper name that English speakers pronounce despite the general restriction.","noteZh":"借词与专名，英语母语者虽有一般限制仍能顺利发音。"},{"text":"[iseʀaq] ‘goose’","noteEn":"A Kalaallisut word whose consonant inventory includes the voiceless uvular plosive [q].","noteZh":"格陵兰语的词，显示该语言的辅音系统包含清小舌塞音 [q]。"}],"body":[{"en":"Physical units may change their pronunciation in some environments, but they may also be refused entry to certain environments altogether. Every language has its own phonotactics: language-specific restrictions on which combinations of units are allowed in which environments. English bans [tl] and [dl] in onsets, yet this is far from universal, since Ngizim has [tlà] ‘cow’ and Hebrew has [dli] ‘bucket’. Other restrictions are looser: English generally lacks [pw] and [vl] onsets, yet speakers pronounce pueblo [pwɛblo] and Vladimir [vlædəmir].","zh":"物理单位在某些环境中会改变读音，但也可能被完全排除在某些环境之外。每种语言都有自己的音位配列，即对本语言中哪些单位组合可出现在哪些环境所作的限制。英语禁止 [tl] 和 [dl] 作音节首，但这远非普遍限制：恩吉齐姆语有 [tlà]（牛），希伯来语有 [dli]（桶）。另一些限制较为宽松：英语一般没有以 [pw] 或 [vl] 起首的音节，但说话者仍能顺利读出 pueblo [pwɛblo] 与 Vladimir [vlædəmir]。"},{"en":"Signed languages show comparable restrictions. In ASL the Symmetry Condition governs signs in which both hands move: such signs must share the same handshape and move in the same way, so the two hands cannot generally do completely different things. The sign SENTENCE obeys the condition, with both hands in the same F handshape wiggling radioularly and tracing a path out to the sides, while the rare exception OPPRESS uses different handshapes on the two hands.","zh":"手语中也有类似的限制。在美国手语中，对称条件约束双手同时运动的手语符号：这类符号必须手形相同、运动方式相同，因此两只手一般不能做完全不同的事。美国手语符号 SENTENCE 符合该条件，两手同为 F 手形，作轻微的桡尺摆动并整体向两侧外移；罕见的例外 OPPRESS 则两手持不同手形。"},{"en":"The pattern of environments in which a unit may occur is its distribution, and determining distributions is a fundamental skill in phonology. The English ban on [tl] and [dl] is not arbitrary: [t] and [d] are both alveolar plosives, so they form a natural class, a set of phones sharing phonetic properties, here place and manner of articulation, and sharing phonological behaviour, here the same phonotactic restriction. Onset clusters work the same way: in a three-consonant onset the first is always [s], the second a voiceless plosive, and the third an approximant.","zh":"某一单位可以出现的环境总和就是它的分布，而判定分布是音系学的基本技能。英语对 [tl] 与 [dl] 的禁止并非任意：[t] 和 [d] 都是齿龈塞音，因而构成自然类，即共享某些语音属性（此处为发音部位与发音方法）并共享某种音系行为（此处为受同一条音位配列限制）的音素集合。音节首辅音丛也是如此：英语的三辅音音节首中，第一个必为 [s]，第二个必为清塞音，第三个必为近音。"},{"en":"Crucially, the membership of a natural class is language-specific, not universal. Although [p], [t], and [k] form a natural class in English, they do not do so in Kalaallisut, also known as Greenlandic, an Inuit language of the Inuit-Yupik-Unangan family spoken in Greenland. Kalaallisut has [p], [t], and [k], but also the voiceless uvular plosive [q], as in [iseʀaq] ‘goose’, so its natural class of voiceless plosives must include all four phones.","zh":"关键在于，自然类的成员因语言而异，并非普遍适用。虽然 [p]、[t]、[k] 在英语中构成自然类，在格陵兰语（Kalaallisut，又称 Greenlandic，属因纽特—尤皮克—尤南干语系，使用于格陵兰）中却不构成自然类。格陵兰语除 [p]、[t]、[k] 外还有清小舌塞音 [q]，如 [iseʀaq]（鹅），因此其清塞音这一自然类必须把四个音素全部纳入，因为自然类必须穷尽。"}]},"chapter-032-slug-4-3-contrastive-distribution-and-minimal-pairs":{"title":{"en":"4.3 Contrastive distribution and minimal pairs","zh":"4.3 对立分布与最小对立对"},"summary":{"en":"Two phones contrast when their distributions overlap, occurring in at least some of the same environments. A minimal pair proves such contrast because two words differ in exactly one position. When minimal pairs are unavailable, near-minimal pairs and speaker judgements about nonce words can serve as evidence.","zh":"当两个音素的分布存在重叠，即至少在某些环境中都能出现时，二者构成对立，形成对立分布。最小对立对能证明这种对立，因为两个词只在某一位置上存在差别。当找不到最小对立对时，可以借助近似最小对立对以及说话人对非词的判断来获取证据。"},"points":[{"en":"Overlapping distributions mean two phones contrast; one minimal pair is enough to prove contrastive distribution.","zh":"两个音素的分布一旦重叠即构成对立；只要找到一例最小对立对，就足以证明它们处于对立分布。"},{"en":"A minimal pair has all the same phones in the same order except at one crucial position.","zh":"最小对立对指两个词除某一关键位置外，所有音素及其排列顺序都完全相同。"},{"en":"Rare phones like English [ʒ] have such limited distributions that minimal pairs are hard to find.","zh":"像英语 [ʒ] 这样罕见的音素分布极受限制，因此很难为其找到最小对立对。"},{"en":"A near-minimal pair has extra differences elsewhere, making it weaker evidence than a true minimal pair.","zh":"近似最小对立对在别处还有额外差异，因此其证据力度弱于真正的最小对立对。"},{"en":"Collecting multiple near-minimal pairs raises confidence that the small differences are incidental.","zh":"收集多个近似最小对立对，可以提高我们对其余微小差异属于偶然、无关判断的信心。"},{"en":"Nonce words fill minimal pair gaps when speakers accept them as possible words of the language.","zh":"非词可以填补最小对立对的空缺，前提是说话人认可其为该语言中可能存在的词。"}],"terms":[{"en":"contrastive distribution","zh":"对立分布","defEn":"Two phones occur in at least some of the same environments, overlapping in distribution.","defZh":"两个音素至少能在某些相同环境中出现，即分布存在重叠。"},{"en":"minimal pair","zh":"最小对立对","defEn":"Two words identical in every phone and position except one crucial position.","defZh":"两个词除某一关键位置外，音素及其顺序完全相同，只在该位置上有别。"},{"en":"near-minimal pair","zh":"近似最小对立对","defEn":"A pair differing at the crucial position but also in one or more other places.","defZh":"在关键位置上存在差别，但在其他一处或多处也同时有别的一对词。"},{"en":"nonce word","zh":"非词（临时编造词）","defEn":"A word made up for one-time use, such as in linguistic experimentation.","defZh":"为一次性使用而临时编造出来的词，常用于语言学实验或测试。"},{"en":"minimal triplet","zh":"最小三连组","defEn":"Three words differing from each other at only one position.","defZh":"三个词彼此只在某一个位置上存在差别的组合形式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[pɪl] pill and [kɪl] kill","noteEn":"A minimal pair: the two words share the form [▁ɪl] and differ in one position.","noteZh":"最小对立对：两个词共享 [▁ɪl] 的形式，只在起始位置上存在差别。"},{"text":"[plɛʒr̩] pleasure and [prɛʃr̩] pressure","noteEn":"A near-minimal pair, since [l] versus [r] differs elsewhere in the word.","noteZh":"近似最小对立对：关键位置之外还存在 [l] 与 [r] 的差别。"},{"text":"[beʒ] beige versus the nonce word [beʃ]","noteEn":"Speakers accept [beʃ] as a possible distinct word, showing [ʒ] and [ʃ] contrast.","noteZh":"说话人认可 [beʃ] 是可能存在的另一个词，说明 [ʒ] 与 [ʃ] 确实构成对立。"},{"text":"beet, bit, bait, bet, bat, but, bot, bought, boat, and boot","noteEn":"A minimal 10-tuplet showing ten vowels contrasting with each other.","noteZh":"最小十连组，表明十个元音彼此之间都存在对立。"}],"body":[{"en":"Besides the distribution of a single phone, phonologists compare the relative distribution of two phones. If some environments allow both, their distributions overlap and the phones are said to contrast, which gives contrastive distribution. The notion adapts the signed-language minimal pair, two signs sharing all articulation except one parameter, to words in spoken languages.","zh":"除单个音素的分布外，音系学还比较两个音素之间的相对分布。若某些环境中二者都能出现，它们的分布便有重叠，称这两个音素互相对立，即处于对立分布。这一概念把手语中「除某一参数外发音动作相同」的最小对立对，推广到口语的词上。"},{"en":"English [p] and [k] share many environments, as in [pɪl] pill and [kɪl] kill, [lɪp] lip and [lɪk] lick, [spɪl] spill and [skɪl] skill. Each pair has all the same phones in the same order except at one position, so [pɪl] and [kɪl] both fit the shape [▁ɪl]. One such pair suffices to establish contrastive distribution, making minimal pairs central to grouping phones into phonemes.","zh":"英语的 [p] 与 [k] 出现在许多相同环境中，如 [pɪl] pill 与 [kɪl] kill、[lɪp] lip 与 [lɪk] lick、[spɪl] spill 与 [skɪl] skill。每一对除某一位置外，音素的数量和顺序都相同，例如 [pɪl] 与 [kɪl] 都符合 [▁ɪl] 的形式。仅凭这样一对词就足以确立对立分布，因此最小对立对是把音素归并为音位的关键依据。"},{"en":"Minimal pairs are not always available. English [ʒ] is the rarest consonant, occurring in [ruʒ] rouge, [ɡərɑʒ] garage, [vɪʒn̩] vision, and [mɛʒr̩] measure but almost never word-initially outside borrowings, proper names, and the neologism [ʒʊʒ] zhoozh. Comparisons with [ʃ] therefore rest on unusual words such as [əluʒn̩] allusion versus [əluʃn̩] Aleutian. When no true minimal pair exists, we rely on near-minimal pairs like [plɛʒr̩] pleasure and [prɛʃr̩] pressure, which also differ in [l] versus [r].","zh":"最小对立对并非总能找到。英语中最罕见的辅音 [ʒ] 出现在 [ruʒ] rouge、[ɡərɑʒ] garage、[vɪʒn̩] vision 和 [mɛʒr̩] measure 等词中，但除借词、专名和新造词 [ʒʊʒ] zhoozh 以外几乎不出现在词首。因此与 [ʃ] 的比较只能依靠 [əluʒn̩] allusion 对 [əluʃn̩] Aleutian 这类生僻词项。当真正的最小对立对不存在时，就改用近似最小对立对，如 [plɛʒr̩] pleasure 与 [prɛʃr̩] pressure，其差别还包括 [l] 与 [r]。"},{"en":"A single minimal pair is powerful evidence, but a single near-minimal pair is not, since the extra differences might themselves matter to the distribution; gathering several increases confidence. Speakers can also judge nonce words invented to fill minimal pair gaps, such as [beʃ] created from [beʒ] beige, and if they accept it as a possible distinct word, the two phones are reasonably taken to contrast. Minimal triplets or larger n-tuplets, like the ten vowels of the words listed above, reduce the work involved.","zh":"单个最小对立对是强有力的证据，单个近似最小对立对却不然，因为那些额外差异本身也可能与分布相关；只有累积多个才能提高信心。说话人还能判断为填补空缺而编造的非词，例如由 [beʒ] beige 造出的 [beʃ]；若该形式被认可为可能存在的另一个词，即可合理认定二者构成对立。最小三连组乃至更大的 n 连组，如上述十个元音构成的组合，能大幅减少所需的工作量。"}]},"chapter-033-slug-4-4-complementary-distribution":{"title":{"en":"4.4 Complementary distribution","zh":"4.4 互补分布"},"summary":{"en":"Two phones are in complementary distribution when their environments never overlap. Such phones may belong to different phonemes, as with English [h] and [ŋ], or to the same phoneme as allophones, as with long [iː] and short [i]. Phonetic similarity helps decide between these two analyses.","zh":"当两个音素出现的环境从不重叠时，它们处于互补分布。这样的音素可能分属不同音位，如英语的 [h] 与 [ŋ]；也可能作为音位变体同属一个音位，如长元音 [iː] 与短元音 [i]。判断这两种分析要靠语音相似性。"},"points":[{"en":"Complementary distribution means each phone has its own set of environments, which never overlap.","zh":"互补分布指两个音素各有一套出现环境，且这两套环境从不重叠。"},{"en":"Contrastive distribution proves separate phonemes, but it is not required for two phones to be separate phonemes.","zh":"对立分布足以证明两个音素分属不同音位，但分属不同音位并不要求必须存在对立分布。"},{"en":"English [h] and [ŋ] are in complementary distribution yet belong to different phonemes.","zh":"英语的 [h] 与 [ŋ] 处于互补分布，但仍属于两个不同的音位。"},{"en":"Long [iː] and short [i] are in complementary distribution and are allophones of a single phoneme.","zh":"长音 [iː] 与短音 [i] 处于互补分布，却是同一个音位的两个音位变体。"},{"en":"Phonetic similarity, meaning shared articulatory properties, guides the choice between these analyses.","zh":"语音相似性，即发音特征上的共同点，是作出上述取舍的依据。"}],"terms":[{"en":"complementary distribution","zh":"互补分布","defEn":"Two phones occur in completely different, non-overlapping sets of environments.","defZh":"两个音素分别出现在两套完全不同、互不重叠的环境之中。"},{"en":"phonetic similarity","zh":"语音相似性","defEn":"The degree to which phones share articulatory properties such as phonation, place, and manner.","defZh":"音素之间在发声、发音部位、发音方法等发音特征上共有的程度。"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"A phone that is a concrete realization of a particular phoneme.","defZh":"某一音位在实际语音中具体实现出来的音素形式。"},{"en":"phonation","zh":"发声","defEn":"The property of consonants concerning voicing and related laryngeal states.","defZh":"辅音在浊音与否及喉部状态方面的特征，是定义辅音的主要属性之一。"},{"en":"manner of articulation","zh":"发音方法","defEn":"The property describing how airflow is modified in producing a consonant.","defZh":"描述气流在发出辅音时受到何种阻碍或调节的发音特征。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[həˈræs] harass","noteEn":"For these speakers [h] appears at the beginning of a word.","noteZh":"对这些说话人而言，[h] 可以出现在词的起始位置。"},{"text":"[vəˈhɪkjulr̩] vehicular and [ˈviəkl̩] vehicle","noteEn":"The [h] appears in the stressed syllable of one related word but not the other.","noteZh":"[h] 出现在其中一个相关词的重读音节中，而在另一个词里消失。"},{"text":"nonce forms such as ŋəræs and lɒh","noteEn":"Swapping [h] and [ŋ] produces forms that speakers judge ungrammatical.","noteZh":"把 [h] 与 [ŋ] 互换所造出的形式，被说话人判定为不合乎语法。"},{"text":"[biːd] bead versus [bit] beat","noteEn":"Long [iː] occurs before voiced codas; short [i] occurs before voiceless ones.","noteZh":"长音 [iː] 出现在浊辅音韵尾之前，短音 [i] 则出现在清辅音之前。"}],"body":[{"en":"Two phones may stand in complementary distribution, each occupying environments that never overlap. For many English speakers [h] occurs word-initially, as in [həˈræs] harass, or at the start of a stressed syllable, as in [ˌkɒmprəˈhɛnd] comprehend and [ˈt͡ʃaɪldˌhʊd] childhood. The phone [ŋ] occurs only where [h] cannot: in a coda, as in [lɒŋ] long and [fɪŋ.ɡr̩] finger, or at the start of an unstressed syllable, as in [ˈsɪ.ŋr̩] singer. Swapping the two yields ungrammatical nonce forms, so no minimal pair exists and the phones appear not to contrast.","zh":"两个音素也可能处于互补分布，各自占据彼此从不重叠的环境。对许多英语说话人来说，[h] 出现在词首，如 [həˈræs] harass，或出现在重读音节之首，如 [ˌkɒmprəˈhɛnd] comprehend 和 [ˈt͡ʃaɪldˌhʊd] childhood。[ŋ] 只出现在 [h] 不能出现的位置：韵尾，如 [lɒŋ] long 和 [fɪŋ.ɡr̩] finger；或非重读音节之首，如 [ˈsɪ.ŋr̩] singer。把二者互换会造出不合乎语法的非词，因此不存在最小对立对，二者看上去并不构成对立。"},{"en":"Yet [h] and [ŋ] clearly belong to different phonemes, written with different symbols even in broad transcription, so contrastive distribution is sufficient but not necessary for separate phonemes. In most North American pronunciations the [iː] of [biːd] bead and the [i] of [bit] beat are distinct phones, the long one roughly 1.2 to 1.5 times as long. They too are in complementary distribution: [iː] requires a following coda of only voiced consonants, as in [biːd] bead, whereas a voiceless coda consonant yields short [i], as in [bit] beat.","zh":"然而 [h] 与 [ŋ] 显然分属不同音位，即使在宽式标音中也用不同符号记录，可见对立分布足以说明音素分属不同音位，却并非必要条件。在多数北美英语发音中，[biːd] bead 的 [iː] 与 [bit] beat 的 [i] 是两个不同的音素，[iː] 的时长约为 [i] 的 1.2 至 1.5 倍。它们同样处于互补分布：[iː] 后面必须跟只含浊辅音的韵尾，如 [biːd] bead；韵尾辅音中只要有一个清音，就出现短音 [i]，如 [bit] beat。"},{"en":"The two pairs therefore receive different analyses: [h] and [ŋ] are treated as separate phonemes /h/ and /ŋ/, while [iː] and [i] are allophones of one phoneme /i/. Phonetic similarity underlies the decision. Though both are consonants, [h] and [ŋ] differ in phonation, place, and manner of articulation, the main properties defining a consonant. The long and short high front vowels instead share vowel quality in height, backness, rounding, and tenseness, differing only in length. Care is needed: the allophones [ɾ] and [tʰ] of /t/ are both alveolar yet otherwise differ sharply.","zh":"因此这两对音素得到不同的分析：[h] 与 [ŋ] 被处理为彼此不同的音位 /h/ 和 /ŋ/，而 [iː] 与 [i] 则被处理为同一音位 /i/ 的两个音位变体。判断依据是语音相似性。[h] 与 [ŋ] 虽都是辅音，却在发声、发音部位和发音方法上都不相同。长短高前元音则在舌位高低、前后、圆唇和松紧四个方面具有相同的元音音质，只在长度上有别。不过判断仍需谨慎：/t/ 的两个音位变体 [ɾ] 与 [tʰ] 同为齿龈音，其他方面差异很大。"},{"en":"In general, contrastive distribution guarantees separate phonemes, while complementary distribution leaves two possibilities: English [h] and [ŋ] belong to different phonemes, whereas [iː] and [i] belong to one phoneme.","zh":"总之，对立分布意味着两个音素分属不同音位；互补分布则有两种可能，例如英语的 [h] 与 [ŋ] 分属不同音位，而 [iː] 与 [i] 同属一个音位。"}]},"chapter-034-slug-4-5-phonemic-analysis":{"title":{"en":"4.5 Phonemic analysis","zh":"4.5 音位分析"},"summary":{"en":"Phonemic analysis determines the phonemes of a language, their allophones, and each allophone's distribution; the result is a phonemicization. Because phonemes are abstract, several analyses may fit the data, and competing accounts are compared by the principle of simplicity. Georgian laterals demonstrate a six-step procedure ending in phoneme /ɫ/.","zh":"音位分析旨在确定一种语言的音位、各音位的音位变体及其分布，所得整体分析称为音位化。由于音位是抽象概念，同一批数据可能容许多种分析，因此需要依据简约性原则比较不同方案。格鲁吉亚语边音的分析展示了完整的六个步骤，最终得出音位 /ɫ/。"},"points":[{"en":"Phonemic analysis identifies a language's phonemes, their allophones, and each allophone's distribution.","zh":"音位分析要确定一种语言的音位、各音位的音位变体以及每个音位变体的分布。"},{"en":"Languages generally lack a single unique phonemicization, since phones can be divided into phonemes in many ways.","zh":"语言通常不存在唯一正确的音位化方案，因为把音素划分为音位可以有多种方式。"},{"en":"When two analyses both fit the data, the simpler one is preferred under the principle of simplicity.","zh":"当两种分析都符合数据时，依据简约性原则优先选择较简单的那一种。"},{"en":"Step one identifies the phones of interest and groups larger sets by natural classes.","zh":"第一步是确定所关注的音素；若音素较多，还需按自然类加以归组。"},{"en":"Comparing simplified environments reveals whether the phones overlap or stand in complementary distribution.","zh":"对简化后的环境进行比较，即可看出两个音素是对立还是互补分布。"},{"en":"The default allophone occurs in the widest variety of environments and usually represents the phoneme.","zh":"默认音位变体出现在最多样的环境中，通常用它的符号来代表整个音位。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonemic analysis","zh":"音位分析","defEn":"Analyzing a language to determine its phonemes, allophones, and allophonic distributions.","defZh":"对一种语言进行分析，以确定其音位、音位变体以及各变体的分布。"},{"en":"phonemicization","zh":"音位化","defEn":"The overall analysis assigning the phones of a language to phonemes.","defZh":"把一种语言的音素整体归入各个音位的分析结果。"},{"en":"principle of simplicity","zh":"简约性原则","defEn":"The preference for the simpler analysis when competing analyses fit the data equally.","defZh":"当多种分析同样符合数据时，优先采用更简单分析的准则。"},{"en":"default allophone","zh":"默认音位变体","defEn":"The allophone appearing in the widest variety of environments, the elsewhere case.","defZh":"出现环境最为广泛的那个音位变体，即其余情况下的默认形式。"},{"en":"natural class","zh":"自然类","defEn":"A group of sounds sharing phonetic properties that pattern together.","defZh":"在音系行为上具有共同表现、共享某些语音特征的一组音。"},{"en":"secondary articulation","zh":"次要发音","defEn":"An additional constriction superimposed on a sound's primary articulation.","defZh":"在主要发音之外附加的另一个收紧动作，如软腭化。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[vxlet͡ʃh] 'I split'","noteEn":"Provides the environment x▁e for the clear lateral [l].","noteZh":"为清边音 [l] 提供 x▁e 这一环境。"},{"text":"[leɫo] 'goal'","noteEn":"Contains both phones: a word-initial environment for [l] and e▁o for dark [ɫ].","noteZh":"同时包含两个音素：[l] 的词首环境与暗 [ɫ] 的 e▁o。"},{"text":"[lif] leaf versus [fiɫ] feel","noteEn":"English shows clear [l] word-initially and dark [ɫ] word-finally.","noteZh":"英语中清 [l] 位于词首，暗 [ɫ] 位于词尾。"},{"text":"[aɫq’a] 'siege'","noteEn":"Only dark [ɫ] occurs before consonants, confirming the prediction.","noteZh":"辅音前只出现暗 [ɫ]，印证了分析所作的预测。"}],"body":[{"en":"Phonemic analysis establishes a language's phonemes, their allophones, and each allophone's distribution; the finished analysis is a phonemicization. Phones may be divided into phonemes in many ways, so no language has just one possible phonemicization, and since phonemes are abstract an analysis cannot be directly verified. Where competing analyses both fit the data, the principle of simplicity favours the simpler one.","zh":"音位分析要确定一种语言的音位、各音位的音位变体及每个变体的分布，完成后的整体分析称为音位化。把音素划分为音位可以有多种方式，因此任何语言都不只有一种可能的音位化方案；又因音位是抽象概念，我们无法直接检验分析是否正确。当两种分析都符合数据时，简约性原则倾向于较简单的一种。"},{"en":"The method can be shown with the Georgian lateral approximants, clear [l] and velarized dark [ɫ], which differ in whether the tongue back is raised. First identify the phones of interest, grouping larger sets by natural class if useful; then list the environment of every occurrence word by word. Thus [vxlet͡ʃh] 'I split' supplies x▁e for [l], and [leɫo] 'goal' supplies environments for both phones. The third step checks for overlap, which would indicate contrastive distribution, as English [p] and [k] would; Georgian shows none.","zh":"这一方法可用格鲁吉亚语的边音来说明：清 [l] 与软腭化的暗 [ɫ]，差别在于舌背是否抬起。先确定所关注的音素，必要时把较大的音素集合按自然类归组；再逐词列出每次出现的环境。于是 [vxlet͡ʃh]「我劈开」为 [l] 提供 x▁e，[leɫo]「目标」则同时为两个音素提供环境。第三步检查环境是否重叠，重叠即意味着对立分布，正如英语 [p] 与 [k] 的情形；格鲁吉亚语的数据中没有这种重叠。"},{"en":"The fourth step simplifies the lists. The left environments vary with no consistent natural class, while the right environments group clearly, so the left side can be ignored. The reduced lists show [l] only before the front vowels [e] and [i], and [ɫ] only before the back vowel [o], the central vowel [a], the voiceless fricatives [ʃ], [s], and [x], and the end of a word. These opposite environments are classic complementary distribution, and since the laterals share phonation, place, and manner, differing only in secondary articulation, they count as allophones of one phoneme.","zh":"第四步是简化环境清单。两个音素的左侧环境纷繁多样，找不出前后一致的自然类，右侧环境却能各自形成清楚的类别，因此可以忽略左侧。简化后的清单显示：[l] 只出现在前元音 [e] 和 [i] 之前；[ɫ] 只出现在后元音 [o]、央元音 [a]、清擦音 [ʃ]、[s]、[x] 之前以及词末。这些恰好相互对立的环境正是典型的互补分布；又因两个边音在发声、发音部位和发音方法上相同，只差次要发音，足以视为同一音位的音位变体。"},{"en":"The final step chooses the default allophone. Since [ɫ] occurs in many dissimilar environments, it is the elsewhere case, and convention uses its symbol to represent the phoneme, giving /ɫ/. Phonemes are abstract and possibly mental, while allophones are concrete measurable sounds, so the bracketing matters. The phoneme /ɫ/ corresponds to [l] before front vowels and [ɫ] elsewhere, as in the diagram of Figure 4.1; this predicts that [aɫq’a] 'siege' can only contain dark [ɫ].","zh":"最后一步确定默认音位变体。由于 [ɫ] 出现在许多彼此不同的环境中，属于其余情况下的默认形式，而按惯例用它的符号代表音位，故记作 /ɫ/。音位是抽象的、可能属于心理表征的实体，音位变体则是具体可测的语音，因此括注方式不可混用。音位 /ɫ/ 对应 [l] 与 [ɫ]，其中 [l] 出现在前元音之前，[ɫ] 出现在其余环境，见图 4.1 的树形图；由此预测 [aɫq’a]「围攻」中只能是暗 [ɫ]。"}]},"chapter-035-slug-4-6-another-example-of-phonemic-analysis":{"title":{"en":"4.6 Another example of phonemic analysis","zh":"4.6 音位分析的另一个实例"},"summary":{"en":"This section works through a fuller phonemic analysis using French data, where six phones of interest form three voiced-voiceless pairs of sonorants. Following the same six steps used for Georgian, it shows that [m] and [m̥] are in complementary distribution and are allophones of /m/, then repeats the procedure for [l]/[l̥] and [ʀ]/[ʀ̥]. The parallel results raise the question of why all three sonorants pattern alike.","zh":"本节以法语材料展示一个更完整的音位分析。六个待考察音素组成三对清浊对应的响音。作者沿用格鲁吉亚语的六个步骤，先分析 [m] 与 [m̥]，发现二者处于互补分布，是同一音位 /m/ 的音位变体，再对 [l]/[l̥] 和 [ʀ]/[ʀ̥] 重复同一程序。三个音位呈现完全平行的模式，由此引出为何全部响音表现一致的问题。"},"points":[{"en":"Six phones of interest in French form three voiced-voiceless pairs: [m]/[m̥], [l]/[l̥], and [ʀ]/[ʀ̥], all sonorant consonants.","zh":"法语中六个待考察音素组成 [m]/[m̥]、[l]/[l̥]、[ʀ]/[ʀ̥] 三对清浊对应的响音。"},{"en":"Listing each phone's environments shows no exact matches, so [m] and [m̥] are not in contrastive distribution but in complementary distribution.","zh":"[m] 与 [m̥] 出现的环境没有完全重合，说明二者不处于对立分布，而处于互补分布。"},{"en":"Voiceless [m̥] occurs only word-finally right after a voiceless obstruent, while voiced [m] occurs elsewhere as the default allophone.","zh":"清音 [m̥] 只出现在紧接清阻塞音之后的词末位置，浊音 [m] 则作为默认音位变体出现在其他环境。"},{"en":"The same steps applied to [l]/[l̥] and [ʀ]/[ʀ̥] yield parallel analyses, since the three pairs form a natural class.","zh":"对 [l]/[l̥] 和 [ʀ]/[ʀ̥] 重复同样的步骤得到平行的分析结果，因为三对音素构成一个自然类。"},{"en":"Each phoneme still has its own separate statements, leaving redundant descriptions that Section 4.7 sets out to eliminate.","zh":"分析仍为每个音位分别列出陈述，留下明显冗余，4.7 节将着手消除这一问题。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phoneme","zh":"音位","defEn":"An abstract sound unit of a language, whose allophones vary predictably by environment.","defZh":"语言中的抽象语音单位，其音位变体依环境不同而可预测地变化。"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"A predictable phonetic variant of a phoneme that appears in a particular environment.","defZh":"某一音位在特定环境中出现的、可以预测的语音变体，同一音位的变体呈互补分布。"},{"en":"complementary distribution","zh":"互补分布","defEn":"The distribution in which two phones never occur in the same environment.","defZh":"两个音素从不出现在相同环境中的分布关系，通常说明它们是同一音位的音位变体。"},{"en":"sonorant","zh":"响音（sonorant）","defEn":"A class of speech sounds produced with relatively open airflow, including nasals and liquids.","defZh":"气流通道相对开放的语音类别，包括鼻音和流音等，在音节中通常充当韵核。"},{"en":"default allophone","zh":"默认音位变体","defEn":"The allophone pronounced when no rule applies to a phoneme in its environment.","defZh":"当音位所处环境没有触发任何规则时所读出的音位变体，也就是该音位的本来读音。"},{"en":"phonation","zh":"发声","defEn":"The voicing state of a sound, whether the vocal folds vibrate or not.","defZh":"语音的清浊状态，即声带是否振动；清响音与浊响音的区别即在于发声。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[ʀym] 'cold/flu' and [film] 'film'","noteEn":"Voiced [m] is word-final only when it is preceded by [y] or by [l].","noteZh":"浊音 [m] 只在 [y] 或 [l] 之后才能出现在词末。"},{"text":"[ʀitm̥] 'rhythm' and [ʀymatism̥] 'rheumatism'","noteEn":"Voiceless [m̥] is word-final only when it is preceded by [t] or by [s].","noteZh":"清音 [m̥] 只在 [t] 或 [s] 之后出现在词末。"},{"text":"[ʀymatismal] 'rheumatic' and [ʀymatism̥] 'rheumatism'","noteEn":"Both phones occur after [s], but [m] only when the vowel [a] follows.","noteZh":"[m] 与 [m̥] 都出现在 [s] 之后，但 [m] 之后还须接元音 [a]。"},{"text":"[pœpl̥] 'people' and [ɔ̃kl̥] 'uncle'","noteEn":"Voiceless [l̥] appears word-finally right after a voiceless obstruent, never elsewhere.","noteZh":"清音 [l̥] 出现在紧接清阻塞音之后的词末位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"The French data in this section present six phones of interest: the voiced sonorants [m], [l], and [ʀ], and the voiceless sonorants [m̥], [l̥], and [ʀ̥]. They follow the same six-step procedure used for Georgian, beginning with one pair and then cycling back to repeat the steps for the remaining phones.","zh":"本节的法语材料涉及六个待考察音素：浊响音 [m]、[l]、[ʀ] 与清响音 [m̥]、[l̥]、[ʀ̥]。分析沿用格鲁吉亚语的六个步骤，先取一对音素入手，再回头对余下的音素重复同样的步骤。"},{"en":"The phones split neatly into three voiced-voiceless pairs, and the analysis starts with [m] and [m̥]. Listing the individual environments shows no exact matches, but some partial similarities. Both occur after [s]: voiced [m] only before the vowel [a], as in [ʀymatismal] 'rheumatic', while voiceless [m̥] only at the end of the word, as in [ʀymatism̥] 'rheumatism'. Both also occur word-finally, but [m] only after [y] or [l], as in [ʀym] 'cold/flu' and [film] 'film', and [m̥] only after [t] or [s], as in [ʀitm̥] 'rhythm'.","zh":"六个音素整齐地分成三对清浊对应的音素，分析从 [m] 与 [m̥] 开始。逐一列出各自出现的环境后可以看到，两份清单没有完全相同的环境，但存在部分相似之处。二者都出现在 [s] 之后：[m] 只出现在元音 [a] 之前，如 [ʀymatismal]「风湿的」；[m̥] 只出现在词末，如 [ʀymatism̥]「风湿病」。二者也都出现在词末，但 [m] 只出现在 [y] 或 [l] 之后，如 [ʀym]「感冒」和 [film]「电影」；[m̥] 只出现在 [t] 或 [s] 之后，如 [ʀitm̥]「节奏」。"},{"en":"Because the two phones occupy different environments, they are in complementary distribution rather than contrastive distribution. [m̥] occurs only word-finally when immediately preceded by a voiceless obstruent, whereas [m] occurs after voiced phones or before any phone at all. Since they are phonetically similar bilabial nasal stops differing only in phonation, they are analysed as allophones of a single phoneme /m/, with [m] as the default allophone because it occurs in more than one environment.","zh":"两个音素分布的环境不同，因此处于互补分布而非对立分布。[m̥] 只出现在紧接清阻塞音之后的词末位置，[m] 则出现在浊音之后或任何音之前，即不出现在词末。二者在语音上高度相似，都是双唇鼻塞音，仅发声（清浊）不同，因此被分析为同一音位 /m/ 的两个音位变体；由于 [m] 出现在多种不同环境中，它是默认音位变体。"},{"en":"The same procedure applied to [l] and [l̥] and then to [ʀ] and [ʀ̥] yields parallel analyses: /l/ and /ʀ/, each with a voiceless allophone word-finally after a voiceless obstruent and a voiced default. Since all three pairs are sonorant consonants, this shared pattern is treated as a natural class and used to predict the behaviour of the last pair. Yet the analysis remains redundant, a problem taken up in Section 4.7.","zh":"对 [l] 与 [l̥]、[ʀ] 与 [ʀ̥] 重复同样的步骤，得到彼此平行的分析结果：/l/ 和 /ʀ/ 各有一个出现在清阻塞音后词末位置的清音位变体，以及一个浊的默认音位变体。由于三对音素都是响音辅音，这种共同的模式被看作一个自然类，并据此预测最后一对音素的表现。不过，这样得到的分析仍然逐音位列出了规则，存在冗余，这一问题将在 4.7 节解决。"}]},"chapter-036-slug-4-7-phonological-rules":{"title":{"en":"4.7 Phonological rules","zh":"4.7 音系规则"},"summary":{"en":"The French analysis leaves many redundant statements, so this section introduces three ways to reduce them: the principle of faithfulness removes default 'elsewhere' statements, natural classes collapse parallel statements into one, and the principle of simplicity chooses the analysis with the fewest statements. It then presents the notation for phonological rules with a target, a change, and an environment, and outlines generative phonology's underlying and surface representations.","zh":"法语的音位分析留下大量重复表述，本节因此介绍三种精简方式：忠实原则消去「其他环境」的默认陈述，自然类把若干平行陈述归并为一条，简单性原则则选取陈述最少的分析。随后给出音系规则的书写形式，说明规则由目标、变化与环境三部分组成，并概述生成音系学中底层形式与表层形式之间的关系。"},"points":[{"en":"The principle of faithfulness lets us delete every default statement, because a phoneme is pronounced as its default allophone elsewhere.","zh":"忠实原则允许删除所有默认陈述，因为音位在其他环境中一律读作其默认音位变体。"},{"en":"Natural classes must be exhaustive, so /n/ and /j/ would belong to any class covering all French sonorants.","zh":"自然类必须是穷尽的，因此任何涵盖法语全部响音的类都应包含 /n/ 和 /j/。"},{"en":"The two competing analyses make different predictions about whether /n/ and /j/ have voiceless allophones, but French phonotactics make this untestable.","zh":"两种分析对 /n/、/j/ 是否有清音位变体做出不同预测，但法语的音位配列使预测无法验证。"},{"en":"The principle of simplicity chooses the single statement: a sonorant is pronounced voiceless word-finally after a voiceless obstruent.","zh":"依简单性原则选择陈述最少的单条规则：响音在清阻塞音后的词末读作清音。"},{"en":"A phonological rule has three components: the target natural class, the change, and the environment C ▁ D.","zh":"音系规则包含三个部分：目标自然类、变化以及环境 C ▁ D。"},{"en":"Generative phonology treats underlying representations as inputs that phonological rules turn into surface representations.","zh":"生成音系学把底层形式视为输入，经音系规则作用后生成表层形式。"}],"terms":[{"en":"principle of faithfulness","zh":"忠实原则","defEn":"The principle that a phoneme is pronounced as its default allophone in any uncovered environment.","defZh":"音位在未被其他陈述覆盖的环境中，一律读作其默认音位变体的原则。"},{"en":"phonological rule","zh":"音系规则","defEn":"A statement that changes a target natural class into allophones in a specified environment.","defZh":"把目标自然类在特定环境中变为相应音位变体的陈述，由目标、变化与环境组成。"},{"en":"natural class","zh":"自然类","defEn":"A group of sounds sharing phonetic properties that pattern together in a language.","defZh":"共享某些语音特征并在语言中表现出相同分布的一组音，且必须是穷尽的。"},{"en":"underlying representation (UR)","zh":"底层形式（underlying representation，UR）","defEn":"The abstract phonemic form of a word, written between slashes.","defZh":"词的抽象音位形式，用斜线括起，作为音系推导的输入。"},{"en":"surface representation (SR)","zh":"表层形式（surface representation，SR）","defEn":"The concrete phonetic form of a word, made of phones and written in brackets.","defZh":"词的具体语音形式，由音素构成，用方括号括起，是推导的输出。"},{"en":"generative phonology","zh":"生成音系学","defEn":"A theory treating underlying forms as inputs that rules convert into surface forms.","defZh":"把底层形式视为输入、由规则转换为表层形式的音系学理论，兴起于二十世纪。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[t͡ʃoli] 'wife' and [xeli] 'hand'","noteEn":"Their underlying representations are /t͡ʃoɫi/ and /xeɫi/, with the phoneme /ɫ/.","noteZh":"二者的底层形式是 /t͡ʃoɫi/ 和 /xeɫi/，其中的清晰 [l] 对应音位 /ɫ/。"},{"text":"[ɛtʀ̥] 'to be', [pœpl̥] 'people', and [ʀitm̥] 'rhythm'","noteEn":"These underlying representations are /ɛtʀ/, /pœpl/, and /ʀitm/, with voiced phonemes.","noteZh":"它们的底层形式分别是 /ɛtʀ/、/pœpl/ 和 /ʀitm/。"},{"text":"sonorant → voiceless / voiceless obstruent ▁ #","noteEn":"The shorthand rule for French sonorants, with target, change, and environment.","noteZh":"法语响音规则的简写形式，依次包含目标、变化与环境三部分。"},{"text":"A → B / C ▁ D","noteEn":"The basic template of a phonological rule, with target A, change B, and environment C ▁ D.","noteZh":"音系规则的基本模板：目标 A、变化 B 与环境 C ▁ D。"}],"body":[{"en":"Written out as pronunciations, the French sonorant analysis gives statements of the form '/X/ is pronounced as [X̥] word-finally after a voiceless obstruent' and '/X/ is pronounced as [X] elsewhere'. The second statement holds for every phoneme, creating massive redundancy. The principle of faithfulness says that a phoneme in an environment covered by no other statement is pronounced the same, so all default statements can be removed, leaving three voiceless statements.","zh":"把法语的响音分析写成发音说明，会得到「/X/ 在清阻塞音后的词末读作 [X̥]」和「/X/ 在其他环境读作 [X]」两类陈述。后一条对每个音位都成立，造成大量冗余。忠实原则指出，若某音位所处的环境未被其他任何陈述覆盖，它就按其本身（默认音位变体）发音；因此可以删去全部默认陈述，只剩下三条清化陈述。"},{"en":"The three remaining statements have exactly the same form, suggesting they belong to one natural class. But a natural class must be exhaustive, and French has other sonorants: [n] and [j] appear in the data and are presumably allophones of /n/ and /j/, so they would have to be included. We therefore face two options: three coincidentally identical statements for /m/, /l/, and /ʀ/, or a single statement covering all sonorants.","zh":"剩下的三条陈述形式完全相同，说明它们可能属于同一个自然类。但自然类必须是穷尽的，而法语中还有其他响音：数据里出现的 [n] 和 [j] 应是 /n/ 和 /j/ 的音位变体，也应纳入其中。于是有两种选择：三条互不相干的陈述恰好形式相同，各自针对 /m/、/l/、/ʀ/；或者存在一条涵盖所有响音的陈述。"},{"en":"The two options predict differently: if /m/, /l/, and /ʀ/ behave independently of /n/ and /j/, those phonemes should have no voiceless allophones; if one pattern covers all sonorants, they should. The data cannot decide, since no relevant /n/ or /j/ words occur, and French phonotactics prevent that anyway. So the principle of simplicity favours the single statement: a sonorant is pronounced voiceless word-finally after a voiceless obstruent.","zh":"两种选择做出不同预测：若 /m/、/l/、/ʀ/ 与 /n/、/j/ 彼此独立，后者在同样环境下不应有清音位变体；若存在统一模式，则 /n/ 和 /j/ 也应有清音位变体。现有数据无法判定，因为其中没有相关环境下的 /n/ 或 /j/，而且法语的音位配列根本不允许出现这种环境。于是依简单性原则选取陈述最少的单条规则：响音在清阻塞音后的词末读作清音。"},{"en":"This statement concerns phonation only, so place and manner must remain faithful and /m/ becomes [m̥] rather than some random voiceless phone. Such statements are phonological rules, written with an arrow for 'is pronounced as', a slash separating change from environment, ▁ for the phoneme's position, and # for word boundaries; a rule therefore has a target, a change, and an environment. Generative phonology treats the underlying representation, made of phonemes, as the input and the surface representation, made of phones, as the output of the rules, a process called a phonological derivation. So [t͡ʃoli] 'wife' and [xeli] 'hand' have the URs /t͡ʃoɫi/ and /xeɫi/.","zh":"该陈述只涉及发声，因此发音部位与发音方法必须保持不变，/m/ 只变为 [m̥]，不会变成任意一个清音。这类陈述称为音系规则，通常用箭头代替「读作」，用斜线分隔变化与环境，用下划线 ▁ 表示音位在环境中的位置，用 # 表示词界；可见规则包含目标、变化与环境三部分。生成音系学把由音位构成的底层形式视为输入，把由音素构成的表层形式视为规则作用后的输出，这一过程称为音系推导。例如 [t͡ʃoli]「妻子」和 [xeli]「手」的底层形式是 /t͡ʃoɫi/ 和 /xeɫi/。"}]},"chapter-037-slug-4-8-phonological-derivations":{"title":{"en":"4.8 Phonological derivations","zh":"4.8 音系推导"},"summary":{"en":"Once the phonemic analysis and the phonological rules are settled, sample derivations of a few critical words demonstrate how the analysis works. The section explains which examples to choose: words showing the rule applying across a representative set of the target natural class, words where the rule fails to apply, and similar sounds in the right environment that remain unaffected. It then shows how to determine underlying representations and how to lay out a derivation table.","zh":"音位分析与音系规则确定之后，可以用几个关键词的样例推导来演示分析如何运作。本节说明应如何挑选例词：既要展示规则在目标处于环境中时正确应用，并覆盖目标自然类中有代表性的若干音位；也要给出规则不适用的例子，以及处于正确环境却不受规则影响的相似音素。随后说明如何依据忠实原则确定底层形式，并介绍推导表的排版方式。"},"points":[{"en":"Sample derivations of a few critical words demonstrate how the phonemic analysis and the rules work.","zh":"用几个关键词的样例推导，演示音位分析与音系规则如何运作。"},{"en":"Show the rule applying to a representative set of the target natural class, with at least one word per phoneme.","zh":"应展示规则在目标自然类中有代表性的音位上正确应用，每个音位至少一个词。"},{"en":"Also show words where the rule fails, and similar sounds in the right environment that stay unaffected.","zh":"还应给出规则不适用的例词，以及处于正确环境却不受影响的相似音素。"},{"en":"Underlying representations differ from surface forms only where a rule applies, so voiceless sonorants become voiced phonemes.","zh":"底层形式只在规则作用处与表层形式不同，因此清响音应还原为对应的浊音位。"},{"en":"A derivation table lists underlying representations on top, rules down the left, and surface representations at the bottom.","zh":"推导表上方列底层形式，左侧列规则，下方列表层形式，并用破折号表示规则不适用。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonological derivation","zh":"音系推导","defEn":"The process by which phonological rules convert underlying representations into surface representations.","defZh":"音系规则把底层形式转换为表层形式的过程，可用推导表展示。"},{"en":"underlying representation (UR)","zh":"底层形式（underlying representation，UR）","defEn":"The abstract phonemic form of a word, used as the input to a derivation.","defZh":"词的抽象音位形式，作为音系推导的输入，用斜线括起。"},{"en":"surface representation (SR)","zh":"表层形式（surface representation，SR）","defEn":"The concrete phonetic form of a word, produced as the output of a derivation.","defZh":"词的具体语音形式，作为音系推导的输出，用方括号括起。"},{"en":"rule application","zh":"规则应用","defEn":"The operation of a phonological rule on a word whose target is in the right environment.","defZh":"当目标音位处于正确环境时，音系规则对其发生作用，否则规则不适用。"},{"en":"principle of faithfulness","zh":"忠实原则","defEn":"The principle that forms stay unchanged except where a rule explicitly applies.","defZh":"形式除规则明确作用之处外保持不变的原理，据此可确定底层形式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[ʀitm̥] 'rhythm', [ɔ̃kl̥] 'uncle', and [ɛtʀ̥] 'to be'","noteEn":"Chosen to show the devoicing rule applying to /m/, /l/, and /ʀ/.","noteZh":"选用它们来展示清化规则分别作用于 /m/、/l/ 和 /ʀ/。"},{"text":"[tabl] 'table'","noteEn":"The rule does not apply: the word-final sonorant follows a voiced sound.","noteZh":"规则不适用：词末响音之前是浊音，因此不发生清化。"},{"text":"[ekʀiʀ] 'to write'","noteEn":"The sonorant follows a voiceless obstruent but is not word-final.","noteZh":"响音虽在清阻塞音之后，却不在词末，故规则不适用。"},{"text":"[limite] 'limited'","noteEn":"A vowel sits in the correct environment but is not a sonorant consonant.","noteZh":"元音处于规则的正确环境中，但不属于响音辅音，因而不受影响。"}],"body":[{"en":"Once the phonemic analysis is complete and the rules are determined, sample derivations of a few critical words demonstrate how the analysis works. The examples should first show the rule applying when the target is in the environment, covering a representative set of phonemes in the target natural class. For French, that means at least one word each with /m/, /l/, and /ʀ/, such as [ʀitm̥] 'rhythm', [ɔ̃kl̥] 'uncle', and [ɛtʀ̥] 'to be'. For a large class such as all obstruents, a few diverse examples suffice: do not choose /t/, /s/, and /ʃ/, but something like /p/, /z/, and /ɡ/.","zh":"音位分析完成、音系规则确定之后，可以通过几个关键词的样例推导来展示分析如何运作。首先应给出规则在目标处于环境中时正确应用的例子，并覆盖目标自然类中有代表性的若干音位。就法语而言，至少要各举一个含 /m/、/l/、/ʀ/ 的词，如 [ʀitm̥]「节奏」、[ɔ̃kl̥]「叔叔」和 [ɛtʀ̥]「是」。若目标自然类很大（如全部阻塞音或全部元音），只需举少量有足够差异的例子；不要用 /t/、/s/、/ʃ/ 来代表所有阻塞音，而应选用 /p/、/z/、/ɡ/ 之类。"},{"en":"It is equally important to show cases where the rule does not apply because the target is in the wrong environment. Good choices are [tabl] 'table', where a word-final sonorant is preceded by a voiced sound, and [ekʀiʀ] 'to write', where a sonorant follows a voiceless obstruent but is not word-final. We may also include a sound similar to the target class that is in the right environment yet remains unaffected: [limite] 'limited' has a vowel in the correct environment, but it does not change, because vowels are not sonorant consonants.","zh":"同样重要的是展示规则因目标处于错误环境而不适用的情况。合适的例子有 [tabl]「桌子」，其中词末响音之前是浊音；以及 [ekʀiʀ]「写」，其中响音虽在清阻塞音之后，却不在词末。此外还可以给出与目标自然类相似、处于正确环境却不受规则影响的音素：[limite]「有限的」中的元音处于规则的正确环境，却不发生变化，因为元音不是响音辅音。"},{"en":"Next we determine the underlying representation of each example word. Because of the principle of faithfulness, the UR and the SR look the same except precisely where a rule applies. Here the only rule creates voiceless sonorants, so we replace every voiceless sonorant in the SRs with the underlying voiced phoneme it derives from, giving /ʀitm/, /ɔ̃kl/, /ɛtʀ/, /tabl/, /ekʀiʀ/, and /limite/.","zh":"接着要确定各例词的底层形式。根据忠实原则，底层形式与表层形式应当相同，只在规则确切作用之处不同。本例中唯一的规则是使响音清化，因此构建底层形式只需把表层形式中的清响音替换为它所来自的浊音位，得到 /ʀitm/、/ɔ̃kl/、/ɛtʀ/、/tabl/、/ekʀiʀ/ 和 /limite/。"},{"en":"Finally we construct a derivation table: the URs and glosses across the top, the relevant rules down the left, and the SRs across the bottom. Each column gives the output of each rule, showing how the word changes, and a dash indicates that the rule does not apply. Naming rules meaningfully also helps, so the French rule is called devoicing.","zh":"最后可以制作推导表：把各例词的底层形式和释义横向列在上方，相关的音系规则纵向列在左侧，表层形式横向列在下方。每一列给出各条规则作用后的输出，显示词发生了怎样的变化；用破折号表示该规则对这个词不适用。给规则起一个有意义的名称也有助于记忆，因此这里把法语响音的规则称为 devoicing（清化）。"}]},"chapter-038-slug-4-9-types-of-phonological-rules":{"title":{"en":"4.9 Types of phonological rules","zh":"4.9 音系规则的类型"},"summary":{"en":"Phonological rules fall into a handful of recurring types. Assimilation is the most common, changing a phoneme to an allophone that shares a property such as voicing, place, or nasality with its environment. Other rules are not assimilatory at all: final devoicing, deletion, and epenthesis. Loanword adaptation shows deletion and epenthesis at work, and familiarity with common rule types guides both phonemic analysis and rule discovery.","zh":"音系规则可分为若干反复出现的类型。最常见的是同化，即音位变为与其环境共享某一特征（如发声、发音部位或鼻音性）的音位变体。也有不少规则与同化无关，例如词末清化、脱落和增音。借词适应体现了脱落与增音的作用；熟悉常见规则类型有助于音位分析与规则发现。"},"points":[{"en":"Assimilation, the most common type, changes a phoneme to an allophone sharing a property with its environment.","zh":"同化是最常见的类型，即音位变为与其环境共享某一特征的音位变体。"},{"en":"Phonation can assimilate from either side: French and Wemba Wemba trigger it from the left, Polish from the right.","zh":"发声同化可来自任一侧：法语和温巴温巴语的触发成分在左边，波兰语的触发成分在右边。"},{"en":"Place and nasality also assimilate: Persian stops become postalveolar, and Ka'apor vowels become nasal after nasal stops.","zh":"发音部位和鼻音性同样会同化：波斯语塞音变为后齿龈音，卡阿波尔语元音在鼻塞音后鼻化。"},{"en":"Non-assimilation rules include final devoicing, deletion of coda /r/, and epenthesis of [e] before Spanish word-initial sC clusters.","zh":"非同化规则包括词末清化、韵尾 /r/ 的脱落，以及在西班牙语词首 sC 组合前增音 [e]。"},{"en":"Knowing common rule types lets analysts ignore unlikely triggers and seek distributional patterns that reveal phonemes.","zh":"了解常见规则类型，可使分析者排除不大可能的音变诱因，并寻找能揭示音位的分布模式。"}],"terms":[{"en":"assimilation","zh":"同化","defEn":"A rule in which a phoneme becomes an allophone sharing a property with its environment.","defZh":"音位变为与其所在环境共享某一特征（如浊音性、发音部位或鼻音性）的音位变体。"},{"en":"final devoicing","zh":"词末清化","defEn":"A rule that makes sounds voiceless at the end of a word.","defZh":"在词末位置使音段失去浊音、变为清音的规则，常作用于阻塞音。"},{"en":"deletion","zh":"脱落","defEn":"A rule that removes a phoneme entirely from a word, shown with the null symbol.","defZh":"把某个音位从词中完全删除的规则，在规则中用空符号 ∅ 表示。"},{"en":"epenthesis","zh":"增音","defEn":"A rule that inserts a new phone into a word, the reverse of deletion.","defZh":"在词中插入一个原本没有的音素以符合音节结构的规则，与脱落恰好相反。"},{"en":"loanword","zh":"借词","defEn":"A word borrowed from one language, the donor, into another, the recipient.","defZh":"从一种语言（施借语）借入另一种语言（受借语），并适应其音系结构的词。"}],"examples":[{"text":"/panpar/ → [panbar] 'shovel'","noteEn":"Wemba Wemba voices a voiceless plosive after a nasal stop, in this word and generally.","noteZh":"温巴温巴语中，清塞音在鼻塞音后浊化，此例即该同化规则的体现。"},{"text":"/rɪbka/ → [rɪpka] 'little fish'","noteEn":"Polish devoices a voiced obstruent when a voiceless obstruent follows it.","noteZh":"波兰语中，浊阻塞音位于清阻塞音之前时发生清化。"},{"text":"/kolomb/ → [kolomp] 'pigeon'","noteEn":"Camuno devoices a word-final obstruent, a common pattern because airflow weakens near the end.","noteZh":"卡穆诺语使词末阻塞音清化；词末气流减弱，因此是清化的自然位置。"},{"text":"/ski/ → [eski] 'ski'","noteEn":"Spanish inserts [e] before word-initial sC so that the cluster does not violate its phonotactics.","noteZh":"西班牙语在词首 sC 前增音 [e]，以免该组合违反音位配列限制。"}],"body":[{"en":"Languages draw on a limited set of recurring phonological rule types. The most widespread is assimilation, in which a phoneme becomes an allophone copying some property already present in its environment. French devoicing is one instance: sonorants lose their voicing in a context that itself contains voicelessness. The same rule can work in the opposite direction, as in Wemba Wemba, where voiceless plosives become voiced after nasal stops, so /panpar/ surfaces as [panbar]. Polish shows that the triggering property need not lie on the left: a voiced obstruent becomes voiceless before a following voiceless obstruent, turning /rɪbka/ into [rɪpka].","zh":"语言所采用的音系规则类型有限且反复出现。最常见的是同化，即一个音位变为音位变体，并复制其环境中已经存在的某一特征。法语的清化即为一例：响音在本身含有清音的语境中失去浊音。同类规则也可朝相反方向起作用，如温巴温巴语（Wemba Wemba）中清塞音在鼻塞音后浊化，/panpar/ 因而实现为 [panbar]。波兰语则表明触发特征未必位于左侧：浊阻塞音在其后接清阻塞音时清化，/rɪbka/ 变为 [rɪpka]。"},{"en":"Phonation is not the only property that assimilates. In Persian, alveolar stops become postalveolar before a postalveolar sound. In Ka'apor, vowels are nasalized after a nasal stop, so /uruma/ is realized as [urumã]. Place and nasality thus spread from a neighbouring segment just as voicing does.","zh":"能够同化的并不限于发声特征。在波斯语中，齿龈塞音位于后齿龈音之前时变为后齿龈音。在卡阿波尔语（Ka'apor）中，元音在鼻塞音后发生鼻化，/uruma/ 实现为 [urumã]。可见发音部位与鼻音性和浊音一样，都可以从相邻音段扩散而来。"},{"en":"Many rules are not assimilatory at all. Final devoicing turns obstruents voiceless at the end of a word, as in Camuno /kolomb/ surfacing as [kolomp]; this is natural because airflow weakens as a word proceeds. Deletion removes a phoneme outright, written with the null symbol ∅, so non-rhotic English varieties lose coda /r/ and /kɑr/ 'car' sounds like [kɑ]. Epenthesis does the reverse by inserting a phone. Borrowings into Spanish illustrate this: [sC] is not a valid onset, so /ski/ and /sloɡan/ are adapted as [eski] and [esloɡan], the epenthetic [e] providing a coda for the /s/.","zh":"还有大量规则与同化无关。词末清化使阻塞音在词末失去浊音，如卡穆诺语 /kolomb/ 读作 [kolomp]；这很自然，因为气流在词内逐渐减弱。脱落则直接删除某个音位，用空符号 ∅ 表示；非儿化英语变体脱落韵尾 /r/，因此 /kɑr/ 'car' 听起来像 [kɑ]。增音与之相反，是插入一个音素。借入西班牙语的词可说明这一点：[sC] 不是合法的音节首，故 /ski/ 和 /sloɡan/ 被改造为 [eski] 和 [esloɡan]，增生的 [e] 为 /s/ 提供了韵尾。"},{"en":"Because rule types recur, knowing them gives analysts a head start. If a language has paired voiced and voiceless sonorants, it is worth testing whether their distribution matches a voicing rule such as assimilation, while properties like vowel rounding can be set aside as unlikely triggers. Rule discovery and phonemic analysis therefore reinforce each other.","zh":"由于规则类型反复出现，了解它们能让分析者抢占先机。若某种语言存在成对的清浊响音，就值得检验其分布是否符合同化一类涉及浊音的规则，而元音圆唇等特征则可作为不大可能的诱因暂时搁置。规则发现与音位分析因此相互促进。"}]},"chapter-039-slug-4-10-signed-language-phonology":{"title":{"en":"4.10 Signed language phonology","zh":"4.10 手语音系学"},"summary":{"en":"Signed languages have fundamentally different modalities from spoken languages, so it is unclear whether they have fully productive phonological rules of the spoken kind. The section explains why such rules may be absent, then describes several rule-like processes that affect individual two-handed signs: weak hand freeze, weak hand drop, lowering, and shifts in the joints used, called distalization and proximalization.","zh":"手语与口语的模态根本不同，因此手语是否具有口语那种完全能产的音系规则尚不确定。本节解释这类能产规则可能缺失的原因，并介绍若干作用于个别双手手势的类规则过程：弱手冻结、弱手脱落、下移，以及所使用关节的转移，即远端化与近端化。"},"points":[{"en":"Spoken phonological rules are fully productive, applying to every form that meets the target and environment, with no exceptions.","zh":"口语的音系规则完全能产，只要满足目标与环境条件就一律适用，没有例外。"},{"en":"Signed languages seem to lack such productive rules, perhaps because they have no unit between phonetic properties and syllables or whole signs.","zh":"手语似乎没有这类能产规则，原因或许在于其语音特征与音节或整个手势之间不存在中间单位。"},{"en":"Rule-like processes in signed languages affect only individual signs; two-handed signs are especially prone because they demand complex articulation.","zh":"手语中类规则的过程只影响个别手势；双手手势因发音复杂而尤其容易发生变化。"},{"en":"Weak hand freeze stops the nondominant hand from moving, while weak hand drop omits it altogether and so resembles deletion.","zh":"弱手冻结使非优势手停止运动，弱手脱落则完全不用该手，因此类似脱落。"},{"en":"Lowering articulates a sign at a lower location, and distalization or proximalization shifts which joints along the arm are used.","zh":"下移把手势改在较低的位置发出；远端化或近端化则改变手臂上所使用的关节。"}],"terms":[{"en":"modality","zh":"模态","defEn":"The channel through which a language is expressed, spoken or signed.","defZh":"语言借以表达的通道，分为口语的听觉—发声模态与手语的视觉—手势模态。"},{"en":"handshape","zh":"手形","defEn":"One of the parameters of a sign, describing the configuration of the hand.","defZh":"手语的参数之一，指打手势时手部所呈现的具体形状或构型。"},{"en":"weak hand freeze","zh":"弱手冻结","defEn":"A process in which the nondominant hand of a two-handed sign stops moving.","defZh":"在双手手势中，非优势手（弱手）停止运动而不随之移动的过程。"},{"en":"weak hand drop","zh":"弱手脱落","defEn":"A process that omits the nondominant hand of a two-handed sign entirely.","defZh":"完全省略双手手势中非优势手（弱手）的过程，可视为一种脱落。"},{"en":"distalization","zh":"远端化","defEn":"A shift of the joints used in a sign toward the fingers.","defZh":"手语中手势所用关节向手指方向移动，即更靠近手部末端的现象。"},{"en":"proximalization","zh":"近端化","defEn":"A shift of the joints used in a sign up the arm toward the shoulder.","defZh":"手势所用关节沿手臂向肩部方向移动，即更靠近躯干的现象。"}],"examples":[{"text":"ASL SENTENCE (two-handed movement) vs. SENTENCE (with weak hand freeze)","noteEn":"The two-handed ASL sign SENTENCE has one form where the nondominant hand moves and one where it is frozen.","noteZh":"ASL 手势 SENTENCE 有两种双手形式：一种非优势手随之运动，另一种非优势手被冻结。"},{"text":"ASL CHOOSE (two-handed) vs. CHOOSE (with weak hand drop)","noteEn":"This ASL sign has a two-handed version with an immobile nondominant hand and a one-handed version.","noteZh":"该 ASL 手势既有非优势手静止的双手形式，也有省略该手的单手形式。"},{"text":"ASL KNOW (at forehead) vs. KNOW (with lowering)","noteEn":"The ASL sign KNOW is made at the forehead but may be lowered to a position under the eyes.","noteZh":"ASL 手势 KNOW 通常在额头处打出，但也可下移到眼睛下方。"},{"text":"ASL CHAT (proximal) vs. CHAT (distal)","noteEn":"One variant of CHAT uses elbow and shoulder movement, the other uses radioulnar movement.","noteZh":"CHAT 的一种变式使用肘部与部分肩部运动，另一种使用桡尺关节运动。"}],"body":[{"en":"Signed languages differ from spoken languages in modality, which raises the question of whether they have phonological rules at all. They do have rule-like processes, but not of the same kind. Phonological rules in spoken languages are fully productive: a French sonorant devoicing rule applies to every sonorant in the right environment, without exception. Signed languages appear to lack rules of this sort.","zh":"手语与口语在模态上根本不同，因此手语是否具有音系规则成为一个问题。手语确有类规则的过程，但性质并不相同。口语的音系规则是完全能产的：法语的响音清化规则适用于处在正确环境中的每一个响音，毫无例外。手语似乎没有这类规则。"},{"en":"One explanation is that signed languages may have no levels of analysis equivalent to phonemes and phones. They have parameters such as handshape and movement, and syllable-like structures, but perhaps nothing in between. In a spoken language a combination of phonetic properties yields just a phone, whereas in a signed language a similar combination already yields a syllable or a whole sign. There may therefore be no suitable unit for phonological rules to target.","zh":"一种解释是，手语可能没有相当于音位和音素的层面。手语有手形、运动等参数，也有类似音节的结构，但二者之间或许空无一物。在口语中，若干语音特征的组合只形成一个音素；而在手语中，类似的组合已经构成一个音节乃至整个手势。因此，可能并不存在适合音系规则作用的单位。"},{"en":"Nevertheless, signed languages show processes that behave somewhat like rules, except that they affect individual signs rather than every sign meeting the conditions. Two-handed signs are frequent targets because they require so much articulatory effort and coordination. In weak hand freeze, the nondominant hand of a moving two-handed sign stops moving. In weak hand drop, an immobile nondominant hand is simply not used, which amounts to a kind of deletion. Lowering places a sign at a lower location, as when KNOW moves from the forehead to under the eyes.","zh":"尽管如此，手语仍表现出一些与规则相似的过程，只不过它们只影响个别手势，而非所有符合条件的手势。双手手势需要大量的发音努力与协调，因而常成为作用对象。弱手冻结指在双手均移动的手势中，非优势手停止运动。弱手脱落则完全不使用静止的非优势手，相当于一种脱落。下移把手势改在较低位置发出，例如 KNOW 由额头移到眼睛下方。"},{"en":"Signs can also change which joints are involved. A shift down the arm toward the fingers is distalization; a shift up toward the shoulder is proximalization. Without knowing a sign's original form, it may be hard to decide which process produced two observed variants. The ASL sign CHAT, for instance, has a more proximal variant using elbow and a little shoulder movement and a more distal variant using radioulnar movement. Modality thus shapes what a phonology can contain, and signed languages must be analyzed in their own right.","zh":"手势还可以改变所使用的关节。关节沿手臂向手指方向下移称为远端化，向肩部方向上移称为近端化。若不知道手势的原始形式，往往难以判断两个变式由哪一种过程造成。例如 ASL 手势 CHAT 既有使用肘部与少量肩部运动的较近端变式，也有使用桡尺关节运动的较远端变式。模态由此决定了音系能够包含什么，手语必须按其自身特点来分析。"}]}});
